\par\par \b \uc2 South Korea  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves sharply drop in May on strong dollar, market  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 185 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juni 2023\par 23:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, June 5 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves declined by the most in eight months in May, weighed down by a strong dollar and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The total value of the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves stood at $420.98 billion at the end of last month, down $5.70 billion from April, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday. It was the biggest monthly decline since September 2022.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Korea\uc2  said in a statement the fall was affected by measures to ease volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, an apparent reference to market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while the converted value of non-dollar assets also fell on a stronger dollar.\par \par \uc2 The South Korean won ended May with a monthly gain of 0.79% against the dollar, after touching its weakest level since late November.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar index, which measures the greenback's value against six major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , rose 2.52%. (Reporting by Jihoon Lee; Editing by Sriraj Kalluvila) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-6-4T22:00:00.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230604ej64014nx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
