                               \par Date of fiscal year end:                                October 31 \par                                                         \par Date of reporting period:                               October 31, 2022 \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Item 1. Reports to Stockholders.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 abrdn Asia-Pacific Income Fund, Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (FAX)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Annual Report\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 October 31, 2022\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 abrdn.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Managed Distribution Policy (unaudited)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Board of Directors of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 abrdn Asia-Pacific Income Fund, Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (the "Fund") has authorized a managed distribution policy ("MDP") of paying monthly distributions at an annual rate set once a year. The Fund's current monthly distribution is set at a rate of $0.0275 per share. With each distribution, the Fund will issue a notice to shareholders and an accompanying press release which will provide detailed information regarding the amount and estimated composition of the distribution and other information required by\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the Fund's MDP exemptive order. The Fund's Board of Directors may amend or terminate the MDP at any time without prior notice to shareholders; however, at this time, there are no reasonably foreseeable circumstances that might cause the termination of the MDP. You should not draw any conclusions about the Fund's investment performance from the amount of distributions or from the terms of the Fund's MDP.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Distribution Disclosure Classification (unaudited)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Fund's policy is to provide investors with a stable distribution rate. Each quarterly distribution will be paid out of current income, supplemented by realized capital gains and, to the extent necessary, paid-in capital.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Fund is subject to U.S. corporate, tax and securities laws. Under U.S. tax rules, the amount applicable to the Fund and character of distributable income for each fiscal period depends on the actual exchange rates during the entire year between the U.S. Dollar and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in which Fund assets are denominated and on the aggregate gains and losses realized by the Fund during the entire year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Therefore, the exact amount of distributable income for each fiscal year can only be determined as of the end of the Fund's fiscal year, October 31. Under Section 19 of the Investment Company Act of\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1940, as amended (the "1940 Act"), the Fund is required to indicate the sources of certain distributions to shareholders. The estimated distribution composition may vary from month-to-month because it may be materially impacted by future income, expenses and realized gains and losses on securities and fluctuations in the value of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in which Fund assets are denominated.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The distributions for the fiscal year ended October 31, 2022 consisted of 27% net investment income, 0% net realized gains and 73% tax return of capital.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In January 2023, a Form 1099-DIV will be sent to shareholders, which will state the final amount and composition of distributions and provide information with respect to their appropriate tax treatment for the 2022 calendar year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 abrdn Asia-Pacific Income Fund, Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Letter to Shareholders (unaudited)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dear Shareholder,\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 We present the Annual Report, which covers the activities of \f28 \uc2 \f2 abrdn Asia-Pacific Income Fund, Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (the "Fund"), for the fiscal year ended October 31, 2022. The Fund's principal investment objective is to seek current income. The Fund may also achieve incidental capital appreciation.\f28 \par