\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea cenbank sold net $15.41 bln for  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2  in Q2\b0\par\par\uc2 136 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2022\par 09:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, Sept 30 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday it sold a net $15.41 billion in the second quarter for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market - its largest sum on record - to soften the won's decline.\par \par \uc2 It was the fourth straight quarter \uc2 the Bank of Korea\uc2  net sold dollars in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and the biggest amount since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began its quarterly release in the third quarter of 2019.\par \par \uc2 The Korean won ended the second quarter with a 6.6% loss against the dollar, which was about the same pace seen in the rise of the U.S. dollar index. (Reporting by Jihoon Lee Editing by Mark Heinrich) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-9-30T08:06:23.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220930ei9u012yv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
