\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Indonesia's rupiah drops, shares rise after rate cut\b0\par\par\uc2 608 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 2020\par 09:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Graphic: World \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://tmsnrt.rs/2egbfVh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://tmsnrt.rs/2egbfVh}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts rates by 25 bps \par     * Rupiah down 0.7% \par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cuts rates by 25 bps\par     * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Thai \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par gains\par \par     Nov 19 (Reuters) - Indonesia's rupiah fell more than half a\par percent and shares gained as the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cut\par rates to support its economic recovery, while Asian stock\par markets struggled for traction on rising COVID-19 cases and\par restrictions.\par     Singapore and South Korea pared losses over\par the day, although Asia's emerging markets drifted as the world\par struggles to keep a lid on infections.  \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia (BI) \f28 \uc2 \f2 cut its seven-day reverse repurchase\par rate by 25 basis points to 3.75%, the lowest since\par BI began using the instrument as its benchmark in 2016, defying\par a majority of economists who predicted no change in policy.\par \par     However, markets were divided through the morning leading up\par to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's decision, on expectations that BI may look\par to stem the rupiah's recent strong gains over November to\par support the economy out of a recession.\par     "Our forecast is that the rupiah will stabilise over the\par coming months, helped by a shrinking current account deficit,\par low inflation and an improvement in global risk appetite,"\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Capital Economics\f28 \uc2 \f2 , who predicted a cut, said in a note after the\par decision.  \par     Indonesia's high-yielding debt is a favourite of foreign\par investors. The yield on the benchmark 10-year bonds\par was unmoved after the decision. \par      The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  unexpectedly cut its policy\par rates by 25 basis points to guide the country's economy through\par the coronavirus crisis.\par     The peso closed slightly lower, and stocks in Manila\par  tracked the broader fall in risk appetite.\par     Broadly, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the region were weaker. South Korea's\par won slid 1% after dealers told Reuters the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was suspected of buying dollars on Thursday to stem gains.\par \par     Fresh from Wednesday's warning of the Thai baht's\par strength and its impact on exports, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it had\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dipped 0.2%.\par     Recent vaccine news from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Pfizer\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Moderna\par , while triggering initial market boosts, have done\par little to assuage investors' concerns that the new wave of\par COVID-19 cases would dent any momentum for a global economic\par recovery.\par     DBS analysts said emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are unlikely to\par be spared from traders looking to cover their shorts, as\par "investors have found it increasingly difficult to extend the\par euphoria from the US elections and vaccine hopes."\par     \par     HIGHLIGHTS:\par     ** Indonesian 3-year benchmark yields fell 1.7 basis points\par to 4.908%\par     ** \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hong Leong Bank Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Public Bank Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par  led losses in Malaysian financials \par     ** Tokyo raises coronavirus alert for infections to highest\par level     \par             Asia stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 0740 GMT\par  COUNTRY      \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RIC      \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       INDEX    STOCKS   STOCKS\par                           DAILY %  YTD %            DAILY %  YTD %\par  Japan                    +0.01    +4.61            -0.36    8.36\par  China                    -0.20    +5.95            0.47     10.26\par  India                    -0.10    -3.89            -0.08    6.24\par  Indonesia                -0.71    -1.91            0.54     -11.30\par  Malaysia                 -0.18    -0.09            -1.11    -0.11\par  Philippines              -0.09    +4.90            -0.77    -10.46\par  S.Korea                  -1.06    +3.66            0.07     15.91\par  Singapore                -0.16    +0.03            0.01     -13.47\par  Taiwan                   +0.89    +5.62            -0.37    14.38\par  Thailand                 -0.20    -1.48            0.53     -13.17\par  \par  (Reporting by Nikhil Kurian Nainan in Bengaluru; Editing by Kim\par Coghill and Ramakrishan M.)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-11-19T09:32:35.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020201119egbj01cj9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
