\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Indonesia's rupiah drops ahead of rate decision, Asia stocks fall\b0\par\par\uc2 603 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 2020\par 05:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Graphic: World \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://tmsnrt.rs/2egbfVh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://tmsnrt.rs/2egbfVh}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     * Indonesia, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  expected to stay on\par hold\par     * Some see room for 25 bps rate cut given recent rupiah\par gains \par     * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Thai \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par gains\par \par     Nov 19 (Reuters) - Indonesia's rupiah fell half a percent on\par Thursday as markets toyed with the possibility of a surprise\par rate cut given its recent strength, while Asian stock markets\par faced downward pressure as COVID-19 cases and restrictions grow.\par     Malaysia led declines in Asia's emerging equity\par markets, falling 1%, while Singapore and South Korea\par  each fell 0.5%, tracking a late sell-off on Wall Street\par as the United States struggles to keep a lid on infections.\par     Economists by and large expect \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  to keep rates\par unchanged at 4% later in the day. However, the rupiah has\par gained over 3% this month alone and some see this as a potential\par trigger for a interest rate cut.\par     "Market expectations are mixed heading into today's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank\par Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  rate decision, divided between a pause and 25bp cut,"\par DBS analysts wrote in a note.\par     The yield on Indonesia's 10-year bonds rose 1.6\par basis points to 6.197% on Thursday, but has fallen sharply since\par the U.S. election week. Yields rise as bond prices fall.\par     Indonesia's high-yielding bonds are a favourite of foreign\par investors.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is also expected to keep rates\par on hold at its meeting later, with the peso little\par changed. Stocks in Manila fell 0.6%.\par     Broadly, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the region were weaker, while South\par Korea's won slid 1% against the dollar after the\par government said it was taking action with stabilise the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par     Dealers told Reuters the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was suspected of\par buying dollars on Thursday to stem gains for a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that has\par gained nearly 3% this month to Wednesday.\par     Fresh from Wednesday's warning of the Thai baht's\par strength and its impact on exports, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it had\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dipped 0.1%.\par     Recent vaccine news from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Pfizer\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Moderna\par , while triggering initial market boosts, have done\par little to assuage investors' concerns that the new wave of\par COVID-19 cases would dent any momentum for a global economic\par recovery.\par     DBS analysts said emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are unlikely to\par be spared from traders looking to cover their shorts, as\par "investors have found it increasingly difficult to extend the\par euphoria from the US elections and vaccine hopes."\par     \par     HIGHLIGHTS:\par     ** Indonesian 3-year benchmark yields fell 1.7 basis points\par to 4.908%\par     ** \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hong Leong Bank Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Public Bank Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par  led losses in Malaysian financials \par     ** Resurgent IDR opens window for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  rate cut\par \par             Asia stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 0342 GMT\par  COUNTRY       \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RIC      \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       INDEX    STOCKS   STOCKS\par                            DAILY %  YTD %            DAILY %  YTD %\par  Japan                     +0.08    +4.68            -0.63    8.08\par  China                     -0.05    +6.11            0.06     9.81\par  India                     +0.00    -3.79            0.00     6.33\par  Indonesia                 -0.50    -1.70            0.32     -11.50\par  Malaysia                  -0.22    -0.12            -0.97    0.03\par  Philippines               -0.05    +4.94            -0.59    -10.30\par  S.Korea                   -0.97    +3.75            -0.54    15.20\par  Singapore                 -0.10    +0.08            -0.46    -13.88\par  Taiwan                    +0.89    +5.62            -0.50    14.23\par  Thailand                  -0.13    -1.42            0.58     -13.12\par  \par  (Reporting by Nikhil Kurian Nainan in Bengaluru; Editing by Kim\par Coghill)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-11-19T05:46:03.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020201119egbj00j7p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
