\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Most Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  set to end 2019 on firm note\b0\par\par\uc2 675 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Dezember 2019\par 07:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Taiwan dollar leads gains on Tuesday\par     * S.Korean won top loser in 2019\par     * Thailand's baht leads gains in 2019\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Shriya Ramakrishnan\par     Dec 31 (Reuters) - Most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were set to end the\par year on a firm note, with the Taiwan dollar leading gains on\par Tuesday, as investors cheered fresh developments on the\par Sino-U.S. trade deal front and upbeat factory activity data from\par China.\par     The White House's trade adviser said on Monday the Phase 1\par deal would likely be signed next week, but said confirmation\par would come from President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2  or the U.S. Trade\par Representative.\par     The deal announced earlier this month has alleviated\par concerns about near-term escalation in tensions between the\par world's two top economies - a major sign of relief for\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Asia, most of which ended 2018 in the red.\par     Adding to the upbeat sentiment, data showed factory activity\par in China expanded for a second straight month in December, as\par Beijing's stimulus measures buoyed domestic demand.\par     The Taiwan dollar strengthened 0.5% on Tuesday,\par hitting its best level in more than a year. The trade-reliant\par economy has bucked a regional trend of growth downgrades, helped\par by manufacturers moving production back home from China to avoid\par higher tariffs.\par     China's yuan extended gains to a near three-week\par high, supported by a firmer-than-expected midpoint fixing by the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Volatility was high during the year, with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par breaching the key 7 per dollar level for the first time in over\par a decade in August, as trade tensions intensified. The yuan was \par set for a second straight annual loss.\par     The Singapore dollar edged up 0.1%, while the\par Malaysian ringgit advanced 0.3%.\par     Investor focus will now turn to the fourth-quarter growth\par figures for Singapore, which is forecast to have expanded at a\par slightly faster pace, with economists expecting a pick-up in the\par services sector to compensate for a prolonged manufacturing\par downturn.\par     The Indian rupee ticked up 0.1% but was set for a\par second annual loss. Concerns over a slowdown in growth weighed\par on the rupee this year, with economists stressing on the need\par for more fiscal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Financial markets in the Philippines, Thailand, Indonesia\par and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were closed for holidays. \par     The Philippine peso and the Indonesian rupiah\par were up 0.2% and 0.4% respectively, in light offshore trade.\par     The peso and the rupiah were poised to gain about 3.5% and\par 3.6% respectively this year, with analysts saying these\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  benefited from demand for higher yields in a\par low-interest rate environment. \par     The South Korean won was the region's worst\par performer for the year, weakening 3.5%, while the Thai baht\par  emerged as the top performer, driven by its large\par current account surplus.   \par        \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par  Change on the day at   0533 GMT                  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                Latest bid  Previous day  Pct Move\par  Japan yen              108.640     108.86        +0.20\par  Sing dlr               1.347       1.3485        +0.10\par  Taiwan dlr             30.000      30.135        +0.45\par  Peso                   50.680      50.78         +0.20\par  Rupiah                 13870.000   13920         +0.36\par  Rupee                  71.280      71.31         +0.05\par  Ringgit                4.092       4.1045        +0.31\par  Yuan                   6.978       6.9865        +0.12\par                                                   \par  Change so far in 2019                            \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                Latest bid  End 2018      Pct Move\par  Japan yen              108.640     109.56        +0.85\par  Sing dlr               1.347       1.3627        +1.16\par  Taiwan dlr             30.000      30.733        +2.44\par  Korean won             1156.400    1115.70       -3.52\par  Baht                   29.900      32.55         +8.86\par  Peso                   50.680      52.47         +3.53\par  Rupiah                 13870.000   14375         +3.64\par  Rupee                  71.280      69.77         -2.12\par  Ringgit                4.092       4.1300        +0.93\par  Yuan                   6.978       6.8730        -1.50\par  \par \par  (Reporting by Shriya Ramakrishnan in Bengaluru; Editing by\par Subhranshu Sahu)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2019-12-31T07:14:44.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020191231efcv00gtl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
