\par\par \b \uc2 BUZZ-COMMENT-Asia cbanks will step in to offset Fed's USD downer\b0\par\par\uc2 232 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juli 2019\par 05:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Jerome Powell just dropped a hot potato in the laps of Asian central bankers. His hint of a pre-emptive Fed rate cut dunked the USD, even though it was widely expected. Excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation would not be welcomed by most Asian nations as they grapple with U.S. tariff-induced economic upheaval. \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's won is especially at risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  or a rate cut to arrest its rise, as a trade war brews with Japan . China's yuan has also gained, by a smaller extent than KRW, but that exerts a bigger impact on Chinese exporters already hurt by tariffs on nearly half of U.S. exports. Beijing has reiterated that the yuan will be kept stable and strong, but it's also understood that it won't be allowed to appreciate too much. \uc2 Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has now flagged plans for measures to control capital inflows and encourage more outflows, to counter rapid gains in the THB.\par \par \uc2  If Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  followed the Fed's lead in easing monetary policy, it would by definition weaken the SGD, making exports more competitive. With growth set to slow to a post-GFC low, an off-cycle easing by the MAS is not out of the question.\par \par \uc2 Released: 2019-7-14T03:02:42.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020190711ef7b009ex\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
