\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  dip on Trump's trade war threats\b0\par\par\uc2 686 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 August 2018\par 08:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Adds Indian rupee, Indonesian rupiah, analyst comments)\par     By Patturaja  Murugaboopathy \par     Aug 31 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakened on Friday as\par concerns mounted that the United States would impose fresh\par tariffs on China next week, while sharp declines in the\par Argentina peso also soured risk sentiment. \par     U.S. President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2  said he was ready to impose more\par tariffs on $200 billion worth of goods from China as soon as the\par public comment period on the plan ends next week, Bloomberg News\par reported.\par     The world's two largest economies have applied tariffs to\par $50 billion of each other's goods and the proposed new U.S.\par measures would mean about half of Chinese imports will be\par charged with tariffs by the United States.\par     "If a full-blown trade war kicks off the U.S. dollar is\par likely to gain," said Greg McKenna, chief market strategist at\par CFD and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  provider AxiTrader.\par     The greenback was likely to find support in the current\par environment, with sustainable momentum in the U.S. economy and\par the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  lifting rates, he said.\par     Sharp declines in the Argentina peso and Turkish lira\par were a drag on Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , especially those with higher\par external deficits. \par     The Argentina peso fell 13.12 percent on Thursday despite\par its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  boosting interest rates as investors doubted\par President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mauricio Macri\f28 \uc2 \f2 's ability to tackle the economic\par crisis.\par     The Indian rupee hit a new low of 71 per dollar on\par Friday, while the Indonesian rupiah was hovering near a\par 20-year low. \par     Traders said \f28 \uc2 \f2 India's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was likely sporadically\par selling dollars through state-run banks to prevent a sudden\par sharp fall, but they didn't expect any major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par  \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's won fell 0.4 percent after the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  kept monetary policy unchanged on Friday and\par dampened expectations of further policy tightening this year.\par \par     China's yuan was set for its fifth consecutive\par monthly decline, though August losses were marginal compared\par with a 3 percent decline in both June and July. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's move to revive a "counter-cyclical factor" in its daily\par fixing propped up the yuan this month. \par     Analysts said they expected regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to feel more\par pressure in September due to the trade dispute between the\par United States and China, and economic crises in Argentina and\par Turkey. \par     "With heightened trade tensions threatening to erupt into a\par full-blown trade war, the region is on alert for disorderly\par capital outflows could lead to financial instability, especially\par in countries that have high external debt levels," DBS said in a\par research note.\par     DBS also pointed to Malaysia "where short-term external debt\par is almost as much as foreign reserves, amidst a weakening growth\par outlook after its May election".\par     Malaysian markets were closed on Friday for a national\par holiday.\par     The following table shows rates for Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against\par the dollar at 0559 GMT.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par \par     \par    Change as of  0559                            \par           GMT                               \par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                 Latest  Previous    Pct\par                              bid       day   Move\par   Japan yen              110.980    110.96  -0.02\par   Sing dlr               1.368      1.3674  -0.03\par   Taiwan dlr             30.714     30.711  -0.01\par   Korean won             1113.00    1108.6  -0.40\par                          0                  \par   Baht                   32.720      32.69  -0.09\par   Peso                   53.470      53.43  -0.07\par   Rupiah                 14725.0     14685  -0.27\par                          00                 \par   Rupee                  70.955      70.74  -0.30\par   Yuan                   6.827      6.8440  +0.25\par  *Malaysian markets are closed                   \par  for National day                           \par   Change so far in 2018                          \par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                Latest   End 2017    Pct\par                          bid                 Move\par   Japan yen              110.980    112.67  +1.52\par   Sing dlr               1.368      1.3373  -2.23\par   Taiwan dlr             30.714     29.848  -2.82\par   Korean won             1113.00   1070.50  -3.82\par                          0                  \par   Baht                   32.720      32.58  -0.43\par   Peso                   53.470      49.93  -6.62\par   Rupiah                 14725.0     13565  -7.88\par                          00               