\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Global Markets News of the Day\b0\par\par\uc2 401 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Mai 2018\par 07:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to Disclose \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Details \par  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in a major policy turnaround has decided to gradually disclose details on its veiled \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to enhance transparency and ease lingering U.S. suspicion that it may be manipulating its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to boost exports. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par China Will Not Trade Off Core Interests \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China denied making any concessions to the U.S. to revive its telecommunications giant \f28 \uc2 \f2 ZTE Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2  ., according to a regular Commerce Ministry briefing on Thursday. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Australian Unemployment Rate Rises in April \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's unemployment rate rose to a higher-than-expected seasonally adjusted 5.6% in April from 5.5% in March. Economists had expected an unemployment rate of 5.5%. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Private-Equity Tech Titans Face Off With New Funds \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Two of the largest technology-focused private-equity firms are competing to raise money for what would be their biggest funds, ratcheting up an already heated race for buyouts in the industry. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Small Caps Set New Highs, Outpacing Multinational Peers \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Shares of small U.S. companies climbed to a fresh record Wednesday, reflecting their gains in the recent tax overhaul and signs that U.S. growth once again looks more robust than that from overseas. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 San Francisco Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2   Begins Search for a New Leader \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 San Francisco Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2  said it has begun searching for a successor to President \f28 \uc2 \f2 John Williams\f28 \uc2 \f2  , who is set to become leader of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 New York Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2  next month. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Venezuela's Creditors Are Cutting Its Crude-Oil Lifeline \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A series of court rulings are a major blow to the cash-strapped and increasingly isolated nation at a time when its once-thriving state energy monopoly, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petr\u243\'00\'F3leos de Venezuela\f28 \uc2 \f2  , has been left in tatters after years of mismanagement. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Crypto Enthusiasts Mob New York Conference \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The price of a bitcoin is down more than 50% this year, but enthusiasm for cryptocurrencies and related projects has hardly been dented, judging by the throngs at an annual crypto conference. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SEC Shows Investors What a Cryptocurrency Scam Looks Like \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Washington wants you to know what a cryptocurrency scam looks like-so regulators made one up. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2   Stands Pat for First Time in 13 Meetings \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  unexpectedly left its benchmark interest rate unchanged, citing a more challenging and volatile situation in world economies.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 May 17, 2018 01:00 ET (05:00 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180517ee5h000bo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal