\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 South Korea \highlight\uc2  to Gradually Disclose  \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange Intervention \highlight\uc2  Details\b0\par\par\uc2 By Kwanwoo Jun \par \uc2 446 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Mai 2018\par 04:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 SEOUL -- \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a major policy turnaround has decided to gradually disclose details on its veiled \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to enhance transparency and ease lingering U.S. suspicion that it may be manipulating its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost exports.\par \par \uc2 South Korean authorities had previously opposed any disclosure of their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  for fear that speculative hot money investors might abuse such information for profit and destabilize local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. They stepped in to tame market volatility.\par \par \uc2 The decision, announced jointly by the finance ministry and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  early Thursday, is expected to help boost "the maturity and international credibility" of the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, said Finance Minister \uc2 Kim Dong-yeon\uc2  at an economic policy meeting.\par \par \uc2 Under the new policy, authorities will publicly release net won-dollar trading volumes starting with a March 2019 disclosure of information from the second half of 2018. In September 2019, details from the first half of 2019 will be released, with more frequent disclosures for three-month periods starting in December 2019.\par \par \uc2 The information will be made public via \uc2 the Bank of Korea\uc2  website, it said.\par \par \uc2 South Korea has remained on the \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -manipulation watch list since 2016, as the U.S. has suspected some of its trading partners of having unfairly devalued local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to be more price-competitive in trade.\par \par \uc2 Seoul has denied that it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to boost exports. The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  jumped 13% against the dollar last year.\par \par \uc2 In its latest semiannual report in April, the Treasury did not designate South Korea as a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator while keeping the country on its watch list.\par \par \uc2 The Treasury report urged \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  to disclose its exchange-rate \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  "in a transparent and timely manner" while noting South Korean authorities' notable moves in November and January to slow the won's appreciation against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 South Korea satisfies two of the Treasury's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rigging criteria: a current-account surplus above 3% of its GDP, and a bilateral trade surplus with the U.S. that's above $20 billion. But the country does not meet the third standard that purchases of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  are "conducted repeatedly" and total at least 2% of gross domestic product over a 12-month period.\par \par \uc2 South Korea has been seeking to bolster financial markets from external shocks due to sudden outflows of foreign capital. The country has kept an ample stock of foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, maintaining as many \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -swap lines as possible.\par \par \uc2 Write to Kwanwoo Jun at kwanwoo.jun@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones New