\par\par \b \uc2 Treasury Concerned About Recent SK  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 553 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 April 2018\par 03:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 2105 ET - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains on Treasury's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -manipulation watch list despite the won's 13% jump versus the dollar last year, thanks to the country's trade and current-account surplus. But the agency also flagged \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  concerns. "The won is not notably strong compared to levels it has been over the last couple decades." Meanwhile, "there was a notable and concerning pickup in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " in November and January "that appears to have been for the purpose of slowing won appreciation against the dollar." The greenback this year has been around levels last seen in late 2014 versus the won. "Treasury will continue to monitor closely Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  practices and urges the authorities to report its exchange-rate \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a transparent and timely manner." The pair is steady this morning, like most in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. (kevin.kingsbury@wsj.com; @kevinkingsbury)\par \par \uc2 2019 ET - Some pep might be returning to Australia's property market with successful residential sales at auction rising in all but 2 capital cities in 1Q versus 4Q, says \uc2 CoreLogic\uc2  . Sydney, the country's biggest market, logged the biggest increase with 64% of auctions being successful from 4Q's 58%. Melbourne logged the highest rate at 68.4%, versus 68.1% in 4Q. But nationally, the successful-sales rate fell 10% from a year earlier in 1Q. (james.glynn@wsj.com; @JamesGlynnWSJ)\par \par \uc2 2007 ET - New Zealand firms' earnings forecasts have been falling since mid-2017, and ANZ says that's more a factor of rising costs than cooled revenue hopes. The investment bank isn't worried about the margin pressure and advocates price hikes to offset the expense increases. That, of course, would push up inflation rates--something \uc2 New Zealand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wouldn't oppose. (james.glynn@wsj.com; @JamesGlynnWSJ)\par \par \uc2 1950 ET - As many agree that Thursday's 1Q CPI report from New Zealand won't mean much policy- or other-wise, ANZ says the trend for prices is still higher. A cyclical low in wage inflation has occurred due to skill shortages, meaning pay hikes will pick up, the bank contends. But the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't be in any hurry to act. (james.glynn@wsj.com; @JamesGlynnWSJ)\par \par \uc2 1934 ET - New Zealand's services sector strengthened last month, says \uc2 BNZ\uc2 , with its metric hitting a 14-month high of 58.8. February's reading was 55.3. Despite breaking out of a tight band seen since September, \uc2 BNZ\uc2  says caution is needed as Easter timing and weather could have impacted the results. The report may overstate underlying trends, the bank adds. (james.glynn@wsj.com; @JamesGlynnWSJ)\par \par \uc2 1924 ET [Dow Jones ] New Zealand vegetable prices rose 9.5% in March led by tomatoes, lettuce, cauliflower, cabbage, and broccoli prices, Stats NZ says. Vegetable crops have been affected by a run of storms in recent weeks; lower supply due to bad weather usually means higher prices. Tomatoes rose more than 60%, while lettuce prices were up 20% in the same period, and cauliflower rose 85%. Cabbage prices rose 50%. Overall, food prices rose 1% in March. (james.glynn@wsj.com; Twitter @JamesGlynnWSJ)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 15, 2018 21:05 ET (01:05 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180416ee4g0000h\p