\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 4-U.S., S.Korea to revise trade pact with  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  side-deal, autos concessions\b0\par\par\uc2 833 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2018\par 05:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds South Korea govt comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies)\par \par \uc2 By David Lawder\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON/SEOUL, March 28 (Reuters) - The United States and South Korea agreed to revise their six-year-old trade pact with a side deal to deter competitive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluation by Seoul and with concessions for U.S. autos and pharmaceutical companies, Trump administration officials said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 They told reporters that the deal includes provisions outlined by South Korean officials on Monday, including a 20-year extension of the 25-percent U.S. tariff on pickup trucks and a doubling of the Korean import cap on autos that meet U.S.-specifications to 50,000 per manufacturer per year.\par \par \uc2 The agreement, cobbled together quickly with only a few rounds of negotiations under Trump's threat of withdrawal, will include a side-letter that requires \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  to provide increased transparency of its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with commitments to avoid won devaluations for competitive purposes.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deal, final details of which are still being negotiated between the U.S. Treasury and South Korea's Ministry of Strategy and Finance, is considered a "side letter" that will not be enforceable with trade sanctions.\par \par \uc2 Many U.S. lawmakers, particularly Democrats, had opposed the 2015 Trans-Pacific Partnership trade deal because it had a similar \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation side-agreement that could not be enforced.\par \par \uc2 Nonetheless, the revised U.S.-South Korean Free Trade Agreement, known as KORUS, would be the first U.S. trade deal in force with a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  side-deal, and would not need congressional approval, the officials said.\par \par \uc2 Asked whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  agreement would ensure that South Korea is not declared a manipulator in the \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2 's next \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  report due on April 15, the officials declined to comment, saying such assessments would be made in accordance with Treasury's normal procedures.\par \par \uc2 Improving \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy transparency would mean disclosing the amount of money spent to curb \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market volatility, an official at \uc2 South Korea's finance ministry\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 "It's about time" \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  discloses \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  details, an official said, asking not to be named due to sensitivity of the issue.\par \par \uc2 South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is often suspected of buying or selling dollars to stem sharp fluctuations in the won against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but there are no official figures on how much money is spent on the so-called "smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 While \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  says its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is restricted to smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  both ways, the practice has exposed the country to criticism that it may be devaluing its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sharpen exporters' competitiveness.\par \par \uc2 Earlier in March, South Korean government officials said plans to disclose details of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  are "under review."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been kept on a Treasury \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  "monitoring list" due to its large global current account surplus and U.S. trade surplus. The Treasury's October report urged Korea to "to enhance the transparency of its exchange rate \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 STEEL QUOTAS, TARIFFS\par \par \uc2 The officials confirmed that \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  agreed to cut its steel exports to the United States by about 30 percent in exchange for the rest being excluded from steel tariffs. Korean aluminum producers would still be subject to U.S. President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's 10 percent tariff on aluminum.\par \par \uc2 Other countries also must agree to similar quotas to escape tariffs, but the size of the limits would vary. The United States is negotiating with Canada, Mexico, Brazil, the \uc2 European Union\uc2 , Australia and Argentina.\par \par \uc2 One official said it was "not a one-size fits all kind of thing" and added that the South Korean quota was agreed due to its "unique" position in steel exports. South Korea imports and processes significant amounts of Chinese-made steel, much of which is under anti-dumping and anti-subsidy tariffs.\par \par \uc2 "What will be the same for any country that is out from under the 232 tariff, like with Korea, there will be a hard quota," the official added.\par \par \uc2 South Korea also agreed to amend a government health program that pays premium prices to domestic drug companies in order to ensure a level playing field for U.S. pharmaceuticals producers, the U.S. officials said.\par \par \uc2 In addition to the increased access for American vehicles that meet U.S. but not necessarily South Korean safety standards, the U.S. officials also said they won reductions in non-tariff barriers to U.S. vehicle sales, including elimination of duplicate environmental testing requirements and recognition of U.S. replacement parts standards.\par \par \uc2 Extension of the phase-out period for U.S. pickup truck tariffs to 2041 would ensure that U.S. pickup truck production would not migrate to South Korea as some production moved to Mexico after the \uc2 North American Free Trade Agreement\uc2  eliminated the tariff, the officials said. (Reporting by Cynthia Kim, Shin-hyung Lee; Editing by James Dalgleish and Sandra Maler) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-3-28T04:14:36.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180327ee3r00sh6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
