\par\par \b \uc2 Investors Score Big on Trump-Related Trade in South Korea\b0\par\par\uc2 869 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Dezember 2017\par 11:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2017, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par By Saumya Vaishampayan, Kwanwoo Jun and Ira Iosebashvili \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors are piling into South Korea's won, confident that the country won't weaken its surging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  because it fears being labeled a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  manipulator by the U.S.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The won is up nearly 12% against the dollar this year, making it one of the world's best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and putting it on track to deliver its biggest annual gain in more than a decade. The won recently traded at its highest level against the dollar in more than two years.\par \par \uc2 Money has poured into Korean markets this year despite concerns about the unstable geopolitical conditions on the peninsula. Foreign investors bought a net $3.3 billion worth of Korean stocks and bonds in October after two months of outflows, according to the latest data from \uc2 Australia and New Zealand Banking Group Ltd\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 Improving economic growth, expectations for higher interest rates and a weaker dollar have helped fuel the won's gains. But just as important to investors has been the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's hesitance to rein in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  "has not been anywhere near as \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it has in the past," said Prashant Singh, a senior portfolio manager at \uc2 Neuberger Berman\uc2  who has held won throughout the year. "This has been one of the primary drivers of the won's strength."\par \par \uc2 Some investors and analysts say one reason is that the government is concerned about antagonizing the Trump Administration, even though a strong won can have a dampening effect on the South Korean economy. \uc2 The Bank of Korea\uc2  works closely with the government to smooth out volatility in the won by buying or selling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Since 2016, South Korea has been on a U.S. Treasury Dept. watch list of countries that Washington says put the U.S. at an unfair disadvantage by weakening their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . U.S. goods become less competitive abroad when foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  fall against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Countries on the list, which includes China, Japan, Germany and Switzerland, could eventually face U.S. sanctions if they take actions like persistently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and running a significant trade surplus with the U.S.\par \par \uc2 Bank of Korea officials have suggested that the U.S. watch list has influenced their policy toward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "It would not be true if we say we are not conscious of remaining on the list when we conduct smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a senior Bank of Korea official who supervises \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets said in an interview.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's comments are reassuring to market participants betting on more won strength, said \uc2 Jorge Mariscal\uc2 , emerging markets chief investment officer at UBS Wealth Management.\par \par \uc2 The words indicate "that they are unwilling to push hard against the current market trend," said Mr. Mariscal, who has been buying won and expects it to gain another 2% against the U.S. dollar over the next 12 months.\par \par \uc2 U.S. and Korean trade officials are also in the process or renegotiating a five-year-old pact that has been a target of criticism from President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be hoping that fewer \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  will produce the same results as in Taiwan. The U.S. in October removed Taiwan from its list of trading partners that might be manipulating their exchange rates after saying \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials there had reduced \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Korea\uc2  's last major suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was on Aug. 16, 2016, when it spent at least $1 billion to slow the won's gains, according to Jeon Seung-ji, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at \uc2 Samsung Futures Inc\uc2 . in Seoul. Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's relative inactivity is a departure from past years, when it was quicker to step in and curb a rising \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Korea\uc2  suggested that local financial authorities are trying to walk a fine line between being less \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2  and abiding by its mandate to stabilize volatile market swings.\par \par \uc2 "One thing for sure is that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  always steps in if it needs to take action to tame market volatility," the official said.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Kim Dong-yeon recently warned against the won's steep gains, his first attempts to talk down the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the new government of President \uc2 Moon Jae\uc2 -in was inaugurated in May.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts say the new government may not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as aggressively in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. Unlike his two conservative predecessors, Mr. Moon has called for "a paradigm shift" in economic policy. He wants more of a focus on domestic demand, and smaller firms that are less sensitive to gains in the won's value.\par \par \uc2 Ruchir Sharma, head of Asia-Pacific \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at \uc2 Credit Suisse Group AG\uc2  in Singapore, said the perception among professional investors like hedge funds that Korean authorities aren't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively has given them "good reason to participate" in the won's advance.\par \par \uc2 Write to Saumya Vaishampayan at saumya.vaishampayan@wsj.com, Kwanwoo Jun at kwanwoo.jun@wsj.com and Ira Iosebashvili at ira.iosebashvili@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 December 04, 2017 05:30 ET (10:30 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020171204edc4000w0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
