\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-S.Korea April export growth hits near 6-year high, trade surplus with US falls\b0\par\par\uc2 783 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Mai 2017\par 04:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Exports rise at fastest pace since Aug 2011\par \par \uc2 * April exports +24.2 pct y/y (Reuters poll: +15.3 pct)\par \par \uc2 * April imports +16.6 pct y/y (Reuters poll: +21.0 pct)\par \par \uc2 * Semiconductors, ship exports helped shipments in April\par \par \uc2 * April exports to US rise, trade surplus falls (Adds detail, analyst comment)\par \par \uc2 By Christine Kim and Cynthia Kim\par \par \uc2 SEOUL, May 1 (Reuters) - South Korean exports rose at a much faster-than-expected pace in April, surging for a sixth straight month helped by robust demand for high-tech memory chips and adding confirmation to perceptions of broad recovery in the global economy.\par \par \uc2 Exports to the United States rose in April but South Korea's trade surplus with that country declined on an annual basis over the same period, Monday's data showed, potentially easing concerns Washington may impose protectionist measures that could hurt South Korea's economy - Asia's fourth-largest.\par \par \uc2 U.S. President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said last week in an interview with Reuters that he was seeking to change a free trade deal with South Korea or scrap it entirely.\par \par \uc2 Preliminary data showed April's exports soared 24.2 percent from a year earlier to $51.01 billion, while imports surged 16.6 percent to $37.75 billion to create a $13.25 billion trade surplus, the Ministry of Trade, Industry and Energy said.\par \par \uc2 Exports rose at the fastest pace since August 2011 when they gained 25.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 Shipments to the United States rose 3.9 percent on-year in April, rebounding from a 5.0 percent fall in March, the official breakdown showed. South Korea's trade surplus with the United States was $1.68 billion in April, down from $2.52 billion a year before.\par \par \uc2 Machinery, oil products and household electronics were the main drivers of exports to the United States last month.\par \par \uc2 "If this trend continues, South Korea will have likely escaped one of the criteria for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator designation," said An Ki-tae, an economist at NH Investment & Securities, adding the trade surplus with the United States was likely to fall below $20 billion this year if it kept declining at the current tempo.\par \par \uc2 "The controversy over trade with the United States will probably fade at this rate," he said.\par \par \uc2 A U.S. trade and customs enforcement law enacted last year set out three criteria for identifying manipulation among major trading partners: a "material" global current account surplus, a "significant" bilateral trade surplus with the United States, and persistent one-way \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  is currently in the process of reducing its trade surplus with the United States, Finance Minister Yoo Il-ho said on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, exports to China rose 10.2 percent on-year in April versus a 12.1 percent gain in March. Last month's gain was thanks to the booming construction sector and capital expenditure in China, the data showed.\par \par \uc2 The trade ministry said it was aiming to diversify South Korea's export destinations to reduce reliance on markets such as the United States and China, given persistent downside risks.\par \par \uc2 Overall, semiconductor chip and flat display panel exports boosted headline export performance in April, jumping 56.9 percent and 10.2 percent on-year respectively. Ship exports also lent a hand, soaring 102.9 percent.\par \par \uc2 With the general downturn in the shipbuilding industry, every ship delivery results in spikes in data, but even without the ship deliveries, exports would still have risen 16.8 percent on-year in April, the trade ministry said.\par \par \uc2 "It will be difficult for exports to maintain growth in the 20-percent range, we'll likely see growth slow a bit in the second half of the year as the base effects subside from crude oil products which drove export growth in the first quarter," said Park Sang-hyun, chief economist at HI Investment & Securities.\par \par \uc2 South Korean financial markets are closed on Monday for a public holiday.\par \par \uc2 The average export value per working day was $2.27 billion in April, compared to $2.04 billion in March, according to Reuters calculations.\par \par \uc2 Exports have been gaining since November last year, bolstering economic growth in the first quarter. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data last week showed first-quarter gross domestic product growth was a faster-than-expected 0.9 percent, the quickest in three quarters.\par \par \uc2 Last week, the trade ministry upgraded its export outlook for the year to between 6 and 7 percent growth from 2.9 percent seen previously. (Reporting by Christine Kim and Cynthia Kim; Editing by Eric Meijer) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-5-1T03:11:04.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020170501ed51000um\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
