10 billion, after a $4.37 billion rise in 2015.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not disclose details or confirm traders' suspicions of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities say they conduct market smoothing activities against extreme one-sidedness or herd behaviour in the market.\par \par \uc2 The data, updated monthly, also showed the forwards positions declined considerably over the course of November and December, coinciding with the election of U.S. President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his taking office.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Korea\uc2  declined to comment on the data or whether it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said it was "too hasty" to give meaning to recent movement in the positions.\par \par \uc2 South Korean officials, including the finance minister, have been vehement that the country will not be named as a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator in the \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2 's report on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies of major trading partners expected in April. (Reporting by Yena Park; Writing and additional reporting by Christine Kim; Editing by Kim Coghill) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-2-22T06:33:44.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020170222ed2m006y2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
