\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Trade mixed despite dollar retreat; yuan hits 8-year low\b0\par\par\uc2 758 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 November 2016\par 07:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  sets weak midpoint\par     * Ringgit near 10-mth low on hedging-linked dollar bids\par     * Malaysia c.bank asks foreign banks to refrain from trading\par NDFs\par     * Won up; S.Korea expects Trump to toughen Treasury \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par reporting\par \par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, Nov 16 (Reuters) - Emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were\par mixed on Wednesday as sentiment towards regional units stayed\par bearish on rising expectations of a U.S. interest rate hike in a\par month's time.\par     The recent rout in global bond markets and the dollar rally\par took more of a back seat.  \par     The Chinese yuan once again hit an eight-year low\par as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set a weaker daily guidance rate. \par     Malaysia's ringgit touched a 10-month trough on\par hedging-related dollar demand among foreign investors as the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  asked foreign banks to refrain from trading\par non-deliverable forwards. \par     By contrast, the South Korean won gained as a\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official said Seoul was bracing for tougher\par scrutiny of its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  management from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\par Department\f28 \uc2 \f2  under a Trump administration.  \par     The Taiwan dollar advanced as local shares \par rose and foreign banks cut holdings in U.S. dollars.\par     The greenback stepped back against a basket of six\par major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , while long-term \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  yields eased\par slightly. \par     Still, the retreat is unlikely to last long as\par stronger-than-expected U.S. October retail sales data reinforced\par the outlook for a \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  interest rate hike in\par December.\par     "Some fatigue is seen setting in, given the huge run-up in\par the dollar and steepening of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 UST\f28 \uc2 \f2  curve in the recent week,"\par said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Christopher Wong\f28 \uc2 \f2 , a senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist for Maybank in\par Singapore, referring to \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  yields.\par     "Inflation could come faster than expected, and this could\par potentially lead to greater impetus for the Fed to raise rates."\par     \par     RINGGIT\par     The ringgit fell 0.3 percent to 4.3490 per dollar, its\par weakest since Jan. 22, in thin trading.\par     The Malaysian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  failed to draw support although most\par government bond prices rose.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has asked foreign banks to refrain\par from trading in the offshore non-deliverable forwards market in\par the ringgit, according to a letter sent to banks and seen by \par Reuters.\par     \par     WON\par     The won rose earlier as much as 0.5 percent against the\par dollar, briefly leading gains among emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Earlier, a South Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official said the\par country is working to avoid being labelled a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par manipulator, which could undermine its trading status.\par      The comments spurred speculation that South Korea could may\par face difficulties stemming the won's appreciation to favour\par exports in the future, given Trump's protectionist trade policy\par stance, analysts said.\par     "The authorities may be reluctant to buy dollars for\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , although their recent dollar-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par gave some room," said Jung Sung-yoon, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst\par at Hyundai Futures in Seoul.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities have recently\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  recently to limit the won's downside, traders said.\par The authorities often step in the market to curb its strength\par when it sharply appreciates, according to traders, and have\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to limit the won's downside. The authorities often\par step into the market to curb the won's strength when it\par appreciates sharply. \par \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0457 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                 Latest bid   Previous day  Pct Move\par   Japan yen                   109.06         109.22     +0.15\par   Sing dlr                    1.4144         1.4130     -0.10\par   Taiwan dlr                  31.755         31.870     +0.36\par   Korean won                 1167.10        1170.60     +0.30\par   Baht                         35.42          35.37     -0.14\par   Peso                        49.150         49.170     +0.04\par   Rupiah    