\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  up as US jobs data eases Sept Fed rate hike chances\b0\par\par\uc2 839 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 September 2016\par 07:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Won over 2-week high on stocks; wary of Korea \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par     * Rupiah hits 2-week high on bond inflows\par     * Baht at 2-week low as foreigners sell stocks, bonds\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SEOUL, Sept 5 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par rose on Monday as a softer-than-expected U.S. jobs report caused\par investors to cut bets that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  may raise\par interest rates as early as this month.\par     South Korea's won and Taiwan's dollar \par raced to their strongest level in more than two weeks on foreign\par demand of local equities.\par     The Indonesian rupiah hit a two-week peak on\par bond-related inflows.\par     China's yuan slightly gained although the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set daily guidance rate weaker. \par     The Thai baht failed to join the regional\par appreciation, touching a two-week low, as foreign investors sold\par the country's stocks and bonds on valuation concerns.\par     U.S. employment growth slowed more than predicted last month\par and wages were tepid, data showed on Friday, which could\par effectively rule out a rate hike this month. \par     "The U.S. data cannot raise odds of rate hikes further, so\par EM Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reversed previous losses," said Qi Gao, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strategist for Scotiabank in Singapore.\par     Still, Gao expects the Fed to raise interest rates by 25\par basis points in December, saying: "don't expect aggressive\par buying of local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\par     Most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had slid since Fed Chair\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Janet Yellen\f28 \uc2 \f2  last month said that the case for a rate increase\par had grown stronger in recent months.\par     Richmond Federal Reserve Bank President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jeffrey Lacker\f28 \uc2 \f2  said\par on Friday that the U.S. economy appears strong enough to warrant\par significantly higher interest rates. \par     U.S. Fed Funds futures prices indicated investors were\par pricing in around a 20 percent chance of a September hike, and\par more than a 60 percent chance by the end of year.\par     \par     WON\par     The won advanced 1.1 percent to 1,105.5 per dollar, its\par strongest since Aug. 18.\par     Foreign investors were set to buy Seoul shares for a\par second straight session.\par     The South Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  found further support from\par suspected demand against the Japanese yen from\par offshore funds, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traders said.\par     South Korea's exporters are expected to buy the won for\par settlements ahead of the Full Moon Festival next week.\par     "Companies which have massive foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  holdings are\par likely to dump them ahead of the Chusok. They will not miss any\par rebound (in the dollar)," said a local bank trader in Seoul,\par referring to the holidays from Sept 14 through Sept 17.\par     Caution grew over possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities to stem further strength in the\par best performing emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  so far this year with\par some traders suspecting official dollar purchases.\par     \par     RUPIAH\par     The rupiah rose 0.6 percent to 13,170 per dollar, its\par strongest since Aug. 22.\par     Most Indonesia's government bond prices slid, but\par some long-term debts prices gained with foreign demand.\par     The official Jakarta Interbank Spot Dollar Rate,\par which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  introduced in 2013 to manage exchange\par rate fluctuations, was fixed at 13,197, firmer than the previous\par 13,261.\par     \par     BAHT\par     The baht lost 0.5 percent to 34.72 per dollar, its weakest\par since Aug 22.\par     Bangkok shares fell to a seven-week low, plunging\par nearly 3 percent earlier, as foreign investors were expected to\par turn to net sellers. Last month, local stocks rose to their\par highest since April 2015 on foreign demand.\par     Foreign investors also unloaded the government bonds\par , especially a short-term notes, on the baht's\par weakness.\par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0545 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                  Latest bid   Previous day   Pct Move\par   Japan yen                    103.26         103.99      +0.71\par   Sing dlr                     1.3570         1.3604      +0.25\par   Taiwan dlr                   31.523         31.703      +0.57\par   Korean won                  1105.50        1117.20      +1.06\par   Baht                          34.70          34.55      -0.43\par   Peso                         46.565         46.620      +0.12\par   Rupiah                        13170          13245      +0.57\par  *Rupee  