\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  draws support from BOE easing; focus switches to U.S. jobs\b0\par\par\uc2 880 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 2016\par 07:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Taiwan dlr hits 1-year high on equity inflows, exporters\par     * Won gains on stock inflows; wary of S.Korea \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par     * Rupiah edges up as Indonesia Q2 GDP growth beats forecasts\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, Aug 5 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par rose on Friday and were set to see weekly gains as the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of\par England\f28 \uc2 \f2 's larger-than-expected monetary stimulus helped\par investors keep seeking higher yields in the region while markets\par braced for key U.S. jobs data.\par     Taiwan's dollar hit a near one-year high on equity\par inflows and exporters' demand for settlements with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  not seen stemming its strength yet.\par     The Malaysian ringgit gained following an\par unexpected rise in June exports and overnight rebounds in oil\par prices.  \par     Inflows into South Korea's stock market threatened to drive\par the won past 1,110 per dollar, which traders said the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities were seen defending. The Indonesian\par rupiah edged up as the Southeast Asia's top economy\par grew faster than expected in the second quarter. \par     The BoE on Thursday cut interest rates to a record-low 0.25\par percent and pledged to buy 60 billion pounds ($78.8 billion) of\par government bonds with newly created money. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also\par announced two new stimulus schemes to deal with the economic\par shock dealt by Britain's vote to leave the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par  \par     Investors were awaiting data on U.S. July nonfarm payrolls\par due later on Friday. U.S. employers were predicted to have added\par 180,000 jobs last month, according to a Reuters poll of\par economists.\par     "The BoE's steps were more aggressive than expected. That\par alleviated recent frustration on global policy stimulus," said\par Jung Sung-yoon, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst at Hyundai Futures in\par Seoul, taking the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2 's recent decision to maintain\par bond buying steady as an example of disappointment.\par     "Risky assets, including emerging Asian, could find more\par support if tonight's NFP (non-farm payrolls) is solid, but below\par 200,000," Jung said.\par     A number above that and a surprisingly weak figure could\par hurt regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , he added.\par     Sentiment on most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  grew more\par positive in the last two weeks as investors kept searching\par higher yields in the region with expectations of further global\par stimulus measures, a Reuters poll showed on Thursday.\par  \par     \par     CAPITAL INFLOWS\par     The Taiwan dollar strengthened 0.5 percent to 31.566 per the\par U.S. dollar, its strongest since Aug 11 last year, extending its\par gain so far this week to 1.1 percent.\par     Scotiabank's emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist Qi Gao said\par the Taiwan dollar is seen strengthening further as global\par stimulus could spur more inflows.\par     "We would sell the pair on rallies in the coming sessions\par with a target of 31.25," Gao said, referring to the U.S.\par dollar/Taiwan dollar.\par     He said the won is another beneficiary.\par     The South Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has advanced 0.8 percent\par throughout this week as foreign investors resumed buying shares\par .\par     Caution prevailed over possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South\par Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities to curb the won's strength.\par     On Tuesday, South Korea's vice finance minister said the\par country will take appropriate measures to stabilise the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate if market moves become excessively one-sided, as\par the won hit more than 13-month highs. The\par authorities were also suspected of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that day, with\par traders estimating they bought more than $1 billion.\par     The ringgit has risen 0.8 percent so far this week as oil\par prices gained.\par     India's rupee has risen 0.3 percent so far this\par week as investors welcomed the long-awaited passage of a goods\par and services tax, although concerns remained over the amount of\par work needed to bring the reforms into reality. \par     The Chinese yuan has eased 0.1 percent for the\par week, while sentiment on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remained stable. \par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0520 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                 Latest bid   Previous day  Pct Move\par   Japan yen                   101.10         101.22     +0.12\par   Sing dlr                    1.3407         1.3422     +0.11\par   Taiwan dlr                  31.567         31.710     +0.45\par   Korean won                 1110.90        1114.00     +0.28\par   Baht                         34.82          34.93     +0.32\par   Peso                        46.975         47.020     +0.10\par   Rupiah                       13117          13135     +0.14\par   Rupee                        66.83          66.91     +0.12\par   Ringgit                     4.0330         4.0490     +0.40\par   Yuan                        6.6468         6.6426     -0.06\par                                                              \par   Change so far in 2016                                      \par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                 Latest bid  End prev year  Pct Move\par   Japan yen                   101.10         120.30    +18.99\par   Sing dlr                    1.3407         1.4177     +5.74\par   Taiwan dlr                  31.567         33.066     +4.75\par   Korean won                 1110.90        1172.50     +5.55\par   Baht                         34.82          36.00     +3.40\par   Peso                         46.98          47.06     +0.18\par   Rupiah                       13117          13785     +5.09\par   Rupee                        66.83          66.15     -1.02\par   Ringgit                     4.0330         4.2935     +6.46\par   Yuan                        6.6468         6.4936     -2.30\par   ($1 = 0.7615 pound)\par \par  (Reporting by Jongwoo Cheon; Additional reporting by Roger Tung\par in TAIPEI; Editing by Simon Cameron-Moore)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-8-5T06:52:06.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160805ec8500b1h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
