\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Doubts over BOJ stimulus ease Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 ; ringgit leads on weak oil\b0\par\par\uc2 751 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 August 2016\par 07:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Ringgit falls on weak oil prices; Malaysia bonds slide\par     * Won down after S.Korea's over $1 bln \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Tue\par     * Rupiah dips; Indonesia bonds still rise\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, Aug 3 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par dipped on Wednesday as demand for high yields in the region\par eased due to doubts over whether the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  would further\par increase its monetary stimulus.\par     The Malaysian ringgit underperformed as weak crude\par prices underscored worries about the country's oil and gas\par revenues, spurring capital outflows. \par     The South Korean won slid as traders said the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities were estimated to buy more than $1\par billion on Tuesday to stem the won's strength.\par     Indonesia's rupiah hit a near one-week low,\par tracking softer regional peers.\par     Japan's government on Tuesday approved 13.5 trillion yen\par ($133.6 billion) in fiscal measures to support the world's\par third-largest economy, while speculation emerged that the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may prepare to put the brakes on monetary stimulus.\par  \par     Still, regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were seen supported as the dollar\par stayed near a 6-week lows against a basket of six major\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as expectations for a U.S. interest rate rise shifted\par to later rather than sooner, analysts said.\par     "Risk assets, including emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , are\par seeing some corrections after the recent rallies due to the\par BOJ's disappointment," said Jeong My-young, Samsung Futures\par research head in Seoul, referring to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's last\par week decision to keep bond purchases steady.\par     "But as long as investors maintain belief that the Fed may\par not tighten it policy, the liquidity-driven rally could\par continue."\par         \par     RINGGIT\par     The ringgit fell as most of Malaysia's government bonds\par prices slumped.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's non-deliverable forwards slid\par overnight despite the dollar's broad weakness.\par     "The ringgit continues to see outflows on the back of weaker\par oil prices, despite pockets of keen interest in EM Asia," said\par Stephen Innes, a senior trader for online multi-asset trading\par services Oanda Asia Pacific in Singapore.\par     \par     WON\par     The won eased as caution grew over possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by\par the authorities to curb its strength.\par     On Tuesday, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's vice finance minister said the\par country will take appropriate measures to stabilise the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate if market moves become excessively one-sided.\par  The comment came after the won hit the strongest\par level in more than 13 months.\par     \par     "Overwhelming \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  caution since yesterday and\par global risk-off mode hurt the won," said a foreign bank trader\par in Seoul.\par     "Exporters sold dollars above 1,115 (for the won), but the\par dollar/won is seen trying to find a bottom."\par     Foreign investors were set to become net sellers in Seoul's\par main stock market, after a buying streak that had lasted\par 19 straight sessions.\par     \par     RUPIAH\par     The rupiah eased to 13,116 per dollar, its weakest level\par since July 28.\par     But the downside for the Indonesian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was limited as\par most government bond prices advanced.\par     On Tuesday, Indonesia sold 18 trillion rupiah ($1.4 billion)\par of bonds at an auction, well above the indicative target of 12\par trillion rupiah, the finance ministry's financing and risk\par management office said. \par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0455 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                 Latest bid   Previous day  Pct Move\par   Japan yen                   101.05         100.90     -0.15\par   Sing dlr                    1.3406         1.3403     -0.02\par   Taiwan dlr                  31.697         31.680     -0.05\par   Korean won                 1113.32        1110.00     -0.30\par   Baht                         34.79          34.75     -0.13\par   Peso                        47.000         46.960     -0.09\par   Rupiah                       13115          13095     -0.15\par   Rupee                        66.77          66.73     -0.05\par   Ringgit                     4.0620         4.0300     -0.79\par   Yuan                        6.6284         6.6299     +0.02\par                                                              \par   Change so far in 2016                                      \par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                 Latest bid  End prev year  Pct Move\par   Japan ye