\par\par \b \uc2 Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Slip for Second Day in a Row\b0\par\par\uc2 631 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juli 2016\par 09:25\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE\u8212\'20\'14The yen and the yuan, two heavyweights in the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  arena, have hit fresh lows recently, leading other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region down with them.\par \par \uc2 Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  slipped for a second day in a row on Tuesday despite a mild rally in several of the smaller stock markets in Asia, which may have taken their cue from another record high for U.S. stocks on Monday. When stocks are up, emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have in the past tended to rally due to investors' increased appetite for risk-taking.\par \par \uc2 The Japanese yen earlier fell to 106.32, its lowest against the U.S. dollar in nearly a month, and back to the level it was trading at before the U.K. voted to leave the \uc2 European Union\uc2  late last month, a decision that triggered heavy buying of the yen given its traditional role as a safe-haven in times of market turmoil.\par \par \uc2 The People's Bank of China\uc2  meanwhile set Tuesday's yuan versus U.S. dollar benchmark at its weakest level in nearly six years, though on a daily basis the adjustment was fractional.\par \par \uc2 The yuan traded at a five-year low on Monday in mainland China, reaching a trough of 6.7030 after official trading hours, which end at 4.30pm each day. Traders said they suspected that earlier in the day, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the yuan from crossing the 6.70 level.\par \par \uc2 A Shanghai-based senior trader at a domestic bank said the \uc2 PBOC\uc2 's apparent approach of ignoring the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's performance in after-hours trading is problematic. "We now have a tightly controlled market before 4:30 in the afternoon and a free market after that. It's an unsustainable contradiction," he said.\par \par \uc2 Analysts have suggested that China may be steering the yuan into a slow descent, to help the country's weakening economy. A cheaper \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  makes Chinese goods appear more attractive to foreign buyers.\par \par \uc2 Japan's yen, meanwhile, has been tumbling ever since Prime Minister \uc2 Shinzo Abe\uc2 's victory in parliamentary elections earlier this month. That has spurred hope Mr. Abe could introduce a fresh round of government spending to stimulate growth, alongside further policy easing by the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The yen's weakening, coupled with the gradual slide of China's yuan, has had an adverse impact on the Singapore dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore\uc2 , the city-state's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  relatively stable against its peers. In June, when the Singapore dollar rallied to a one-year high of S$1.3313 against the dollar, traders said there were strong signs that the MAS had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to counter the move.\par \par \uc2 The yen's slide has also had an impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Japan's trade rival, \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 , where the authorities also tend to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to manage the cross-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate. The relative weakness of the won versus the yen contributes to the appeal of choosing South Korean products over their Japanese-made equivalents. Keeping the won relatively weak is thus an imperative for South Korea's government, to support export-based economic growth. The won hit a three-month high versus the dollar on Friday, but has been depreciating since the start of the week.\par \par \uc2 Weakness in key \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the yen and the yuan has also hit more minor \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia. Malaysia's ringgit is down 1.1% compared with Friday, while the Philippine peso is down 0.2%, as is the Indian rupee.\par \par \uc2 Shen Hong contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 July 19, 2016 03:25 ET (07:25 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160719ec7j000xq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
