\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Upbeat China economic growth fuels Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 ; won leads weekly gains\b0\par\par\uc2 831 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 2016\par 08:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Yuan edges up as \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  seen keeping firm hand\par     * Won up on equity inflows; \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  seen near 1,130/dlr\par     * Taiwan dollar at 11-month peak on stock inflows, exporters\par     * Baht over 10-wk high; Thai deputy PM not concerned over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, July 15 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose on Friday as stronger-than-expected Chinese\par economic data further boosted risk sentiment with regional units\par set to enjoy weekly gains, tracking strong equity markets.\par     China's economy grew 6.7 percent in the second quarter,\par slightly faster than forecast, as the government stepped up\par stabilisation efforts. Industrial output and retail sales also\par beat forecasts. \par     "Better-than-expected China data would definitely alleviate\par the residual uncertainty," said Andy Ji, Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strategist for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commonwealth Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Singapore.\par     Ji said the South Korean won, the Taiwan dollar\par  and the Thai baht are expected to strengthen\par with limited downside to their policy interest rates.\par Indonesia's rupiah and Malaysia's ringgit are\par likely to appreciate with valuation advantage, he added.\par     The won led weekly regional gains, hitting a near\par three-month peak, as offshore funds scrambled for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par on sustained equity inflows.\par     Taiwan's dollar touched an 11-month high on continuous stock\par inflows and as traders dumped the U.S. dollar to stop losses.\par Exporters also chased the island's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for settlements in\par panic.\par     The baht rose to its strongest in more than 10 weeks on\par capital inflows and as Thailand's deputy prime minister said he\par was not concerned about the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's strength. \par     China's yuan edged up as state-run banks were\par seen capping the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weakness. \par     Sentiment towards emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was buoyant even\par before China's indicators as regional stocks hit eight-month\par peaks after record highs on Wall Street. A deadly attack, which\par killed up to 80 people and injured scores in the French Riviera\par city of Nice on Thursday, did not deter investors' appetite for\par Asia. \par     "The troubles in Europe whether economic or something else\par are likely to boost demand for Asian assets," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commonwealth Bank\par of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Ji said.\par     \par     WON OUTPERFORMS\par     The won rose 2.5 percent against the dollar so far this\par week, outpacing regional peers, according to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Thomson Reuters\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par data.\par     Earlier on Friday, the South Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose as much as\par 0.6 percent to 1,130.4 per dollar, its strongest since April 20,\par as foreign investors bought more than 2 trillion won ($1.8\par billion) worth of Seoul shares in total, in seven\par consecutive sessions, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Korea Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2  data showed.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities were suspected of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem the won's strength traders said.\par     "They seemed to defend 1,130 today after absorbing sizeable\par dollar offers yesterday," said a foreign bank trader in Seoul.\par     The ringgit has gained 1.8 percent on bond inflows.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Wednesday unexpectedly cut its policy\par interest rate, helping investors seek capital gains\par in the country's bonds. \par     The Malaysian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  eased on Friday as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par governor was quoted on Thursday as saying the first rate cut in\par seven years was not a start of an easing cycle. \par     Taiwan's dollar has appreciated 1.1 percent against the U.S.\par dollar so far this week. The island's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is rarely\par spotted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb strength in the Taiwan dollar,\par traders said. Importers stayed away, expecting more strength in\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The baht has risen 0.8 percent throughout this week, while\par both the Indian rupee and the Philippine peso\par  have gained 0.4 percent.\par \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0620 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                Latest bid   Previous day  Pct Move\par   Japan yen                  105.80         105.35     -0.43\par   Sing dlr                   1.3443         1.3427     -0.12\p