\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Brexit vote burns Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 ; won, Sing dlr to see worst day in 5 yrs\b0\par\par\uc2 869 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 2016\par 08:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Won, Sing dlr could have largest daily losses since late\par 2011\par     * S.Korea suspected of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ; other c.banks say could\par act\par     * Most EM Asia government bond prices up; stocks lose ground\par \par  (Adds S.Korea \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Indonesia comment, updates)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, June 24 (Reuters) - Emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par slid in volatile trade on Friday, driven by a plummeting pound\par and a rush to safe-haven assets as Britain was voting to leave\par the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     The rush began as soon as the "leave" camp took a commanding\par lead in the British referendum.\par     The Singapore dollar and the South Korean won\par  were set to see their worst day in nearly five years,\par although there was some caution over possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par authorities were suspected of stepping into that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par market, traders said.\par     At the start of trading Friday morning Asia time, most\par regional units rose with the won and Malaysia's ringgit \par to near two-month peaks as opinion polls had showed the "Remain"\par supporters gaining momentum.\par     But the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  quickly turned weaker and then extended\par losses as counting of results showed Britain was voting to leave\par the union. \par     The pound hit the lowest in three decades and global\par equities were hit hard. The safe-haven yen jumped more\par than 4 percent and most emerging Asian government bond prices\par rose with South Korea's 10-year government bond yield\par  at a record low.\par     Other emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lost ground with South Africa's\par rand falling almost 8 percent. The Russian rouble \par slid more than 4 percent.\par     Risk assets, including Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , had priced in the\par probability that Britain would vote to stay in the union, and\par sentiment about them could keep being hurt by the Brexit\par decision.\par     "I'm not comparing Brexit to the global financial crisis,\par but in that situation where you have commonalities, where\par markets are nervous, people are avoiding risks, you inevitably\par have a flight to quality," said Andrew Cross, deputy treasurer\par for International Finance Corporation, a unit of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 World Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     "Investors do move to what they perceive to be a risk-free\par asset," said Cross in Singapore.\par     \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par     The Singapore dollar lost 1.5 percent against the U.S.\par dollar by early afternoon. If that holds through the day, Friday\par will have the biggest one-day loss since November 2011,\par according to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Thomson Reuters\f28 \uc2 \f2  data.\par     Traders rushed to dump the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which until recently\par has outperformed. Before Friday, some analysts said the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's nominal effective exchange rate (NEER) was close to\par the top of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's policy band. \par     The city-state's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pared some of its earlier losses\par with growing caution over possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary\par Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore\f28 \uc2 \f2  to limit its losses.\par     \par     WON\par     The won fell to as weak as 1,180.3 per dollar as Seoul\par shares lost more than 4 percent, with foreigners\par selling.\par     South Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities were suspected of\par buying the won around the session low, traders said. \par     Vice Finance Minister Choi Sang-mok said authorities will\par take all necessary measures to stabilise markets following\par Britain's exit from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 EU\f28 \uc2 \f2 , including smoothing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par reduce volatility in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets. \par     Still, the won lost 2.5 percent for the day in the local\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, its largest daily depreciation since September\par 2011.\par     \par     RUPIAH\par     Indonesia's rupiah lost nearly 1 percent as Jakarta\par shares slid over 2.3 percent.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  warned it was prepared to act to\par stem volatility in the rupiah.\par     A Bank Indonesia spokesman said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is always\par in the market and it had prepared steps to take however the UK\par vote came out.\par     Juda Agung, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's executive director of\par monetary and economic policy, said he believed the rupiah's\par reaction is temporary.\par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0605 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                 Latest bid   Previous day  Pct Move\par   Japan yen                   102.40         106.14     +3.65\par   Sing dlr                    1.3579         1.3376     -1.49\par   Taiwan dlr                  32.410         32.190     -0.68\par   Korean won                 1177.08        1150.20     -2.28\par   Baht                         35.40          35.18     -0.62\par   Peso                        46.880         46.535     -0.74\par   Rupiah                       13380          13255     -0.93\par   Rupee                        68.03          67.25     -1.15\par   Ringgit                     4.1050         4.0185     -2.11\par   Yuan                        6.6120         6.5795     -0.49\par                                                              \par   Change so far in 2016                                      \par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                 Latest bid  End prev year  Pct Move\par   Japan yen                   102.40         120.30    +17.48\par   Sing dlr                    1.3579         1.4177     +4.40\par   Taiwan dlr                  32.410         33.066     +2.02\par   Korean won                 1177.08        1172.50     -0.39\par   Baht                         35.40          36.00     +1.69\par   Peso                         46.88          47.06     +0.38\par   Rupiah                       13380          13785     +3.03\par   Rupee                        68.03          66.15     -2.76\par   Ringgit                     4.1050         4.2935     +4.59\par   Yuan                        6.6120         6.4936     -1.79\par