\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won, Taiwan dlr rise before U.S.  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  report; ringgit leads Asia gains\b0\par\par\uc2 939 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 April 2016\par 08:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Stock inflows further support won, Taiwan dollar\par     * S.Korea, Taiwan caution on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remains\par     * Ringgit tracks overnight rise in oil prices\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, April 20 (Reuters) - South Korea's won hit a\par 5-1/2-month high and Taiwan's dollar hovered near an 8-month\par peak on Wednesday as their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities may\par allow more appreciation ahead of a \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  report on\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  practices of major trading partners.\par     Most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  advanced, led by the\par Malaysian ringgit, on the overnight weakness in the\par U.S. dollar. But regional units pared much of their gains with\par oil prices turning lower and Chinese stocks sliding.\par     The won rose as much as 0.7 percent to 1,128.3\par per dollar, its strongest since Nov. 4. The Taiwan dollar\par  gained 0.3 percent to 32.155 to the U.S. dollar,\par compared to a session high of 32.154 on March 31, the strongest\par level since Aug. 14.\par     "The authorities are worried that the forthcoming \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S.\par Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  manipulators report - it usually releases the\par semi-annual reports in April and October - will designate Korea\par a manipulator, which based on an amendment to the customs bill\par could result in tougher measures," said Tim Condon, head of Asia\par research for ING in a note.\par     "We consider Korea and Taiwan easy targets for politicians\par that need to show they're 'doing something.' We are reviewing\par our 1,140 year-end USD/KRW forecast for downward revision," he\par wrote.\par     In October, the Treasury Department concluded that no major\par U.S. trading partner has manipulated exchange rates. But the\par department said signs pointed to an undervalued won and urged\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and be more transparent.\par  \par     Regarding Taiwan, the department said its authorities should\par not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to resist more market pressure for appreciation,\par and should limit \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to exceptional\par circumstances of disorderly market conditions.\par     Traders and analysts say \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities of\par South Korea and Taiwan have been stepping into markets to\par prevent sharp rises in their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from hurting exports,\par their economies' main growth engine.\par     \par     SUBDUED \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par     With growing caution ahead of the U.S. report, authorities\par in those economies have not actively slowed appreciation of\par their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this week, according to the traders and\par analysts. \par      That coincided with a weakening of those two \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par against the yen . Japan is a major\par competitor to South Korea and Taiwan in overseas markets.\par     However, it does not necessarily mean that those authorities\par will let their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  keep rising, traders said.\par     On Wednesday, South Korea's authorities were suspected of\par stemming the won's strength, some traders in Seoul said. The\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has risen 0.7 percent against the dollar on share\par inflows this month after surging 8.2 percent in March, the\par largest monthly gain in seven years.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was also suspected of easing\par appreciation pressure in the domestic \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market on Monday\par and Tuesday, according to traders in the island. The island's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rallied 3.7 percent on equity inflows in March, the\par best performance since February 2008.\par     South Korean government officials said the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  may\par not designate the country a manipulator, given \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par curb the won's depreciation in February when the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hit a\par 5-1/2-year low on capital outflows.\par     Still, those officials remained wary as the United States\par may assess historical \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy.\par     "We would feel fine if they look at only this year. But if\par they assess three, five, or 10 years, we may not feel relieved,"\par a senior \f28 \uc2 \f2 South Korea's finance ministry\f28 \uc2 \f2  official said.\par     \par     RINGGIT\par     The Malaysian ringgit rose, tracking overnight rises in oil\par prices.\par     The ringgit pared some of earlier gains as crude futures\par fell after Kuwaiti oil workers ended a three-day strike that had\par cut production from the Middle Eastern country. Most of\par Malaysia's government bond prices slid.\par     Traders saw the move as short-term profit taking.\par     "Oil price action is very constructive and given the current\par positive risk environment, Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are likely to\par continue strengthening and the MYR should continue to outperform\par the region," said Stephen Innes, a senior trader for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  broker\par OANDA Asia Pacific in Singapore.\par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 545 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                Latest bid   Previous day  Pct Move\par   Japan yen                  108.91         109.21     +0.28\par   Sing dlr                   1.3428         1.3365     -0.47\par   Taiwan dlr                 32.223         32.265     +0.13\par   Korean won                1135.60        1136.30     +0.06\par   Baht                        34.94          34.90     -0.11\par   Peso                       46.135         46.085     -0.11\par   Rupiah                      13135          13145     +0.08\par   Rupee                       66.33          66.55     +0.34\par   Ringgit                    3.8740         3.8905     +0.43\par   Yuan                       6.4662         6.4581     -0.13\par                                                             \par   Change so far in 2016                                     \par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                Latest bid  End prev year  Pct Move\par   Japan yen                  108.91         120.30    +10.46\par   Sing dlr                   1.3428         1.4177     +5.58\par   Taiwan dlr                 32.223         33.066     +2.62\par   Korean won                1135.60        1172.50     +3.25\par   