\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar Pares Gains; South Korean Won Nears 6-Year Lows\b0\par\par\uc2 By Carolyn Cui   \par \uc2 509 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Februar 2016\par 23:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar gave back some of its early gains Friday, as investors took profits on trades by selling the dollar and buying back other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  before heading into the weekend.\par \par \uc2 While the buck managed to hold on to its gains against a number of commodity \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it fell in value versus some of its major rivals. The WSJ Dollar Index, which compares the greenback against a basket of 16 commonly traded \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , edged down 0.2% to 89.06.\par \par \uc2 In afternoon session, the dollar was up against the Australian dollar, the Canadian dollar and the New Zealand dollar, in part due to a continuous slide in oil prices. Prices for the U.S. crude fell 3.7% to settle at $29.64 per barrel.\par \par \uc2 But the dollar continued to weaken against the Japanese yen, a traditional safe-haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , down 0.6% to Yen112.598, despite a broad-based rally in global equity markets.\par \par \uc2 The yen had strengthened as much as 6% against the dollar since the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  joined the negative interest-rate club, a move that has confounded many market participants, raising questions whether there are other forces at play, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 Against the euro, the dollar edged down 0.2% to $1.1130 per euro.\par \par \uc2 Throughout the week, the greenback restored some strength as solid U.S. economic data rolled in, including industrial production, producer prices and weekly jobless claims, adding to the dollar's strength.\par \par \uc2 "Those figures were particularly supportive of the dollar, bolstering the case that the U.S., while it may have shifted to a lower gear at the end of last year, still doesn't appear to be headed to a recession," said Omer Esiner, chief market analyst at \uc2 Commonwealth \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Inc\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Friday, a hotter-than-expected reading of core consumer-price index in the U.S. fueled market expectations for further policy tightening by the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 , adding to the dollar's strength.\par \par \uc2 Among emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Russian ruble and the Malaysian ringgit weakened against the dollar on Friday, down 0.8% and 0.7%, respectively, along with falling oil prices.\par \par \uc2 The South Korean won tumbled to the weakest level in more than five years against the dollar, making it one of the worst performers among all Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The won recently fell 0.3% to 1,232.9 per dollar, the lowest level since June 2010, despite \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The movement of the won was noticeable in a week when the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared relatively stable.\par \par \uc2 Escalating geopolitical tensions in the Korean Peninsula after North Korea's launch of a long-range missile triggered an exodus of foreign capital. "Foreign holders of Korean debt have been selling over the past few sessions, putting pressure on the won," said Brad Bechtel, a managing director at Jefferies LLC.\par \par \uc2 Write to Carolyn Cui at carolyn.cui@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 February 19, 2016 17:28 ET (22:28 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160219ec2j0042j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pich