\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Risk aversion force Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  to see weekly losses; rupee at 2-1/2-year low\b0\par\par\uc2 900 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Februar 2016\par 07:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Rupee down on stock outflows; \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  caution limits\par     * Thai deputy PM says c.bank can manage baht for exports\par     * Foreigners cut Korea bond holdings by $2.6 bln so far 2016\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, Feb 12 (Reuters) - Emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell\par on Friday to see weekly losses as worsening risk sentiment for\par now outweighed expectations of slower U.S. interest rate hikes,\par with investors braced for the reopening of China's markets after\par the Lunar New Year holiday.\par     India's rupee fell to its lowest in nearly 2-1/2\par years on stock outflows, but the decline was halted by caution\par over potential \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the\par worst-performing Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  so far this year.\par     The Thai baht slid as Deputy Prime Minister Somkid\par Jatusripitak said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was able to manage the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to ensure it will not affect exports. That caused\par expectations of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cap further strength in the\par baht.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's won slumped as foreigners continued\par to sell local stocks and bonds. The Malaysian\par ringgit slid on stop-loss selling in non-deliverable\par forwards markets. \par     Asian stocks lost ground as mounting concerns over the\par health of European banks posed more risks to global economic\par growth, which has already been under pressure from falling oil\par prices and a sluggish Chinese economy.\par     Sentiment on the regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could deteriorate\par further if global risk aversion adds to pressure on China's\par financial markets when they reopen on Monday.\par     "Chinese mainland equities will likely open with a heavy\par correction lower and that will lead to CNH weakness," said Heng\par Koon How, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Credit Suisse\f28 \uc2 \f2  private\par banking and wealth management in Singapore, referring to the\par offshore yuan.\par     "The latest negative global developments may force Asian\par central banks to adopt more dovish monetary policies to preserve\par what's left of growth prospects in the region. Therefore, we see\par limited strength in Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  going forward and more likely\par weakness will resume," Heng said.\par     Earlier this week, regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had risen as Federal\par Reserve Chair \f28 \uc2 \f2 Janet Yellen\f28 \uc2 \f2  stressed a 'gradual' rate hike path,\par highlighting global risks to the U.S. economy. \par     Heng said the rise was halted by Asian companies using the \par opportunity to hedge their dollar requirements.\par     \par     FAIL TO KEEP YELLEN'S SUPPORT\par     Most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were set to suffer losses\par during the holiday-shortened trading week.\par     The rupee and the won led regional depreciation with both\par having lost 1.2 percent so far this week.\par     The Indian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  earlier on Friday hit 68.44 per dollar,\par its weakest since September 2013.\par     The won slid as \f28 \uc2 \f2 South Korea's finance ministry\f28 \uc2 \f2  official said\par foreign holdings of the local bonds have fallen by a net 3.2\par trillion won ($2.6 billion) so far this year. \par     Investors were awaiting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's monetary policy\par meeting on Tuesday. \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Korea\f28 \uc2 \f2  is expected to leave\par interest rates unchanged next week, but could cut soon as\par external uncertainties could hurt a fragile recovery at home.\par  \par     "We are still bearish on the KRW in the medium term on\par expectations of more monetary easing, deteriorating portfolio\par inflows and China's slowdown," said Qi Gao, an emerging Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist for Scotiabank in a client note.\par     "We expect the BOK to lower its policy rate sooner rather\par than later to tackle the nation's sluggish growth," Gao said\par referring to South Korea.\par     The ringgit has lost 0.7 percent over the week as investors\par sold into a rally, as last year's worst performing Asian\par emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has become the region's best performer so far\par this year.\par     The baht has eased 0.1 percent so far this week.\par     The Thai deputy prime minister's comments came as the baht\par found support from foreign investors buying local short-term\par bonds. Somkid also said he was not worried about short-term\par inflows to the country.\par \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0600 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct