\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -More stable yuan no joy for Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  yet; oil hits ringgit\b0\par\par\uc2 785 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 2016\par 07:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * China seeks yuan stabilisation, but onshore yuan down\par     * Ringgit falls on sliding oil, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  downgrade\par     * Won at 5-1/2-yr low; to weaken more if it breaks\par 1,213.6/dlr\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, Jan 12 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par turned weaker on Tuesday as China's efforts to stabilise the\par yuan have not yet convinced investors that Beijing has control\par over the recent market turmoil.\par     China set another firm fixing for the yuan and\par stepped up a verbal campaign, backed by what traders said was\par aggressive buying. \par     Analysts said offshore buying by state-owned banks, under\par the direction of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of China (PBOC)\f28 \uc2 \f2 , dried up\par yuan liquidity to such an extent that overnight yuan borrowing\par rates in Hong Kong (HIBOR) hit a record high, and the spread\par between onshore and offshore yuan exchange rates briefly\par evaporated. Last week, the spread had exceeded 2\par percent, making it harder for China to stem capital outflows.\par     "It remains to be seen if the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  can achieve convergence\par without stymieing the offshore market," said Andy Ji, Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commonwealth Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  in\par Singapore.\par     "If the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  doesn't manage to achieve convergence, it will\par suffer further. I see risks of a stronger yuan against the rest\par of Asia because the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  needs to keep the renminbi stable,\par whereas the rest of Asia suffers from broad risk-off over\par uncertainties regarding the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's actions," said Ji.\par     Onshore yuan weakened, putting more pressure on\par the Singapore dollar. The city-state's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  closely\par tracks the renminbi as traders and analysts believe it is\par included in the undisclosed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  basket used by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary\par Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore\f28 \uc2 \f2  to manage monetary policy.\par     The Malaysian ringgit led regional losses on\par sliding oil prices and after \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's Investors Service\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Monday\par cut the country's sovereign rating outlook to stable from\par positive. \par     \par     RINGGIT\par     The ringgit slid as continuous falls in crude prices added\par to concerns over Malaysia's sliding oil and gas revenues.\par Malaysia is a major supplier of palm oil and liquefied gas.\par     Crude prices have slumped as much as 20 percent since the\par beginning of the year. \par     The Malaysian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also came under pressure after\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  slashed the country's rating outlook.\par     "The domestic bond market may turn slightly defensive in\par reaction to the news, but we don't expect large foreign outflows\par as a result of the rating outlook cut by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2 ," said Winson\par Phoon, a fixed income analyst for Maybank Investment Bank in\par Kuala Lumpur.\par         \par     WON\par     South Korea's won started the day firmer, but it\par turned weaker to hit a fresh 5-1/2-year low as a weaker yuan\par prompted offshore funds to rush to sell the won.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  slid to as weak as 1,213.0 per dollar, its\par lowest since July 2010.\par     Caution increased over possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South\par Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities to stem further weakness in\par the worst-performing Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  so far this year.\par     Still, the won is likely to fall further if it weakens past\par a strong chart support level at 1,213.6, the 76.4 percent\par Fibonacci retracement of its appreciation from 2010 to 2014,\par analysts said.\par     The South Korean unit is seen heading to 1,277.0, its low of\par 2010, once the support line is broken, they added.    \par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0520 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       117.47         117.75       +0.24\par   Sing dlr        1.4389         1.4344       -0.31\par   Taiwan dlr      33.433         33.651       +0.65\par   Korean won     1212.20        1209.80       -0.20\par   Baht             36.32          36.28       -0.11\par   Peso             47.39          47.27       -0.25\par   Rupiah        13840.00       13870.00       +0.22\par   Rupee            66.88          66.81       -0.10\par   Ringgit         4.4000         4.3750       -0.57\par   Yuan            6.5741         6.5695       -0.07\par  \par   Change so far in 2016\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       117.47         120.30       +2.41\par   Sing dlr        1.4389         1.4177       -1.47\p