\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korean shares, won fall as weak commodities weigh\b0\par\par\uc2 378 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Dezember 2015\par 03:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * KOSPI drops, profit-taking sets in after days of gains\par     * Won slips, mirroring strength in US dollar overnight\par \par     By Yeonsoo Kwak\par     SEOUL, Dec 18 (Reuters) - South Korean shares fell on Friday\par morning, tracking weakness in global markets as a slump in oil\par prices and profit-taking after a winning streak took their toll.\par     The Korea Composite Stock Price Index (KOSPI) was\par down 0.5 percent to 1,968.36 points as of 0148 GMT, poised to\par end a three-day run of gains. \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  data showed on Friday South Korea's producer\par prices fell in November for a 16th straight month, at the same\par pace as they did in October. \par     "Investors, notably foreigners, took profits following a\par recent three-day rally," said Kim Ye-eun, an analyst at LIG\par Investment & Securities. \par     After oil prices fell, refiners underperformed the broader\par market, whereas airline stocks extended gains on hopes their\par fuel bills will drop. \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 SK Innovation Co Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which owns the country's\par largest refiner \f28 \uc2 \f2 SK Energy Co Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 , shed 1.5 percent,\par while \f28 \uc2 \f2 Asiana Airlines Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2  rose 4.1, hitting its\par highest intra-day level in six weeks.\par     Tech giant \f28 \uc2 \f2 Samsung Electronics Co ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2  fell 1.1\par percent to 1,276,000 won. Automaker Hyundai Motor Co \par lost 0.6 percent. \par     Foreign investors were set to extend their own selling spree\par for a 13th straight session, offloading a net 84.4 billion won\par ($71.3 million) worth of KOSPI shares on the main board. \par     The South Korean won fell, mirroring a rise in the\par dollar, but stemmed some early losses on caution over possible\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities to\par curb the losses.\par     The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was quoted at 1,184.9 per\par dollar, down 0.4 percent, after touching as low as 1,187.0. \par     March futures on three-year treasury bonds gained\par 0.04 points at 109.43. \par     \par                        0148 GMT    Prev close\par  Dollar/won             1,184.9       1,180.1\par  Yen/won             9.6702/866        9.6601\par  *KTB futures            109.43        109.39\par  KOSPI                 1,968.36      1,977.96\par  * Front-month futures on three-year treasury bonds\par \par  (Reporting by Yeonsoo Kwak; Editing by Kenneth Maxwell)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-12-18T03:09:38.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020151218ebci002e8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
