\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  falls as yuan retreats, Fed jitters grow\b0\par\par\uc2 930 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Dezember 2015\par 06:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Rupiah at over 2-month low on year-end corp \f28 \uc2 \f2 USD\f28 \uc2 \f2  demand\par     * Won hits 2-1/2-month trough on foreign stock selling\par     * Ringgit over 3-week low on oil rout, bonds fall\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SEOUL, Dec 14 (Reuters) - Emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell on\par Monday as China's yuan hit a 4-1/2-year low and regional stock\par markets fell on growing nervousness ahead of an expected\par interest rate hike this week by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     The yuan lost as much as 0.2 percent to 6.4665 per\par dollar, its weakest since July 2011, with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par setting its daily guidance rate at a 4-1/2-year low. \par     The China \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Trade System, a unit of the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , announced after the market close on Friday that it\par had launched a new trade-weighted yuan exchange rate index, in a\par move that some traders said may also suggest Beijing will allow\par the renminbi to weaker further in a near term. \par     The decision rekindled some fears of a "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  war" -\par competitive devaluations among Asian central banks to weaken\par their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "We could see other Asian countries counter with their own\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of America Merrill Lynch Global\par Research\f28 \uc2 \f2  in a note.\par     "In particular, the response by KRW, TWD and MYR will need\par to be watched closely and we have been advocating a short \f28 \uc2 \f2 3M\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par equally weighted basket of these \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against \f28 \uc2 \f2 USD\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which\par we believe are most exposed to CNY depreciation," said the note,\par referring to the South Korean won, the Taiwan dollar\par  and the Malaysian ringgit.\par     Falling commodity prices and a firm U.S. dollar ahead of the\par Fed decision on Wednesady also pressured emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Wednesday concludes a two-day policy\par meeting where the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is widely expected to raise\par borrowing costs for the first time in nearly a decade.\par     Some analysts and traders had expected emerging Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to rebound if the Fed suggests further rate increases\par will be at a very gradual pace.\par     Still, regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may not benefit much, given the\par weak outlook for the yuan, analysts said.\par     "Consensus expects a dovish (Fed) hike, but for a meaningful\par relief rally in EM \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to ensue it would probably require a very\par downbeat message," analysts for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Societe Generale\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a note.\par     "Given a dovish hike is very consensus, positioning is not\par stretched and USD-RMB is heading higher, a relief rally seems\par like a low probability."\par     \par     RUPIAH\par     Indonesia's rupiah slid 1 percent to 14,090 per\par dollar, its weakest since Oct. 7, on growing corporate dollar\par demand for year-end payments.\par     The official Jakarta Interbank Spot Dollar Rate,\par which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  introduced in 2013 to manage exchange\par rate fluctuations, was fixed at 14,076, its weakest in more than\par two months.\par     The rupiah pared earlier losses as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was\par spotted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  around 14,100,\par traders said.\par     Bank Indonesia Governor Agus Martowardojo said the authority\par will always be in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to guard against\par volatility. \par     Most of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's non-deliverable forwards \par also strengthened, limiting the spot's downside.\par     \par     WON\par     The won lost nearly 0.8 percent to 1,188.4 per dollar, its\par weakest since Sept. 30.\par     Offshore funds sold the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as foreign investors\par extended their selling spree in Seoul's main stock exchange\par  into a ninth straight session.\par     Foreigners dumped a combined net 2.3 trillion won ($1.9\par billion) in equities during the period, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Korea Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2  data\par showed.\par     The won recouped some early losses on caution over possible\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities to\par stem its losses.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also has a chart support at 1,188.0, the 76.4\par percent Fibonacci retracement of its appreciation from September\par to October, analysts said.\par     \par     RINGGIT\par     The ringgit slumped as much as 0.9 percent to 4.3300 per\par dollar in thin trading, its weakest since Nov. 20, as a global\par crude oil rout underscored worries about Malaysia's falling oil\par and gas revenues.\par     Malaysia's government bond prices also slid.\par     Global oil prices extended losses on a forecast from the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Energy Agency\f28 \uc2 \f2  that global oversupply of oil is\par likely to deepen next year. \par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0400 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       121.16         121.00       -0.13\par   Sing dlr        1.4115         1.4138       +0.16\par   Taiwan dlr      32.893         32.965       +0.22\par   Korean won     1185.90        1179.50       -0.54\par   Baht             36.10          36.05       -0.14\par   Peso             47.34          47.24       -0.22\par   Rupiah        14045.00       13945.00       -0.71\par   Rupee            66.96          66.88       -0.12\par   Ringgit         4.3150         4.2925       -0.52\par   Yuan            6.4588         6.4553       -0.05\par  \par   Change so far in 2015\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       121.16         119.66       -1.24\par   Sing dlr        1.4115         1.3260       -6.06\par   Taiwan dlr      32.893         31.718       -3.57\par   Korean won     1185.90        1099.30       -7.30\par   Baht             36.10          32.90       -8.86\par   Peso             47.34          44.72       -5.53\par   Rupiah        14045.00       12380.00      -11.85\par   Rupee           