\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Hopes on Greece deal support Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 , won at 1-month high\b0\par\par\uc2 817 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 2015\par 07:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Won rises on exporters; wary of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par     * Taiwan dollar at 3-week peak on inflows\par     * Ringgit gains, Malaysian bond prices up\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, June 22 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose on Monday as hopes emerged for a deal to avert a\par debt default by Greece after Athens made new proposals to\par foreign creditors before the emergency euro zone summit later in\par the day.\par     South Korea's won hit a near one-month high on\par exporters' demand for month-end settlements. The Taiwan dollar\par  touched a three-week high as local stocks outperformed\par regional peers, and on inflows from foreign financial\par institutions.\par     The dollar eased against a basket of six major\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  with the euro up after Greek government said\par it had a new plan to secure financial aid and prevent a debt\par default. \par     Still, investors remained cautious about Greece's proposals\par because it was not immediately clear how far Greece had yielded\par to creditors' demands for additional spending cuts and tax\par hikes, nor whether creditors could accept the offer.\par     "Asia has been essentially subject to a risk-off trading\par dynamics on the back of rising European yields as well as the\par concern over Greece," said Sacha Tihanyi, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strategist for Scotiabank, said in a research note.\par     "A Greek-relief result at today's European summit should\par mean USD/Asia lower and a better bid for regional fixed income."\par     A failure could dampen risk sentiment and extend\par underperformance in Asia's risk assets, Tihanyi said.\par     \par     WON\par     The won gained 0.9 percent to 1,097.5 per dollar, its\par strongest since May 26.\par     Caution grew over possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities to stem the won's strength as it\par flirted around chart resistance levels.\par     The South Korean unit has a 120-day moving average at\par 1,098.1. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been closing daily sessions weaker\par than the average since May 26.\par     It also has the 50.0 percent Fibonacci retracement of its\par depreciation from April to June at 1,095.5.\par     \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\par     The Taiwan dollar advanced 1.1 percent to 30.728 per dollar,\par its strongest since June 1.\par     The local stocks jumped 1.3 percent, well outpacing\par a 0.8 percent gain in a broad index of Asia-Pacific shares\par outside Japan.\par     The island's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may strengthen further if the won\par extends its appreciation, traders said.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  closely monitors movements in the won\par for its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy because the island competes against\par South Korea in overseas markets for some key products such as\par semiconductors.\par     The Taiwan dollar pared some of earlier daily gains on\par importers' demand of the U.S. dollar for payments.\par     \par     RINGGIT\par     The ringgit rose as Malaysian government bond prices rose.\par     The 10-year yield fell to 4.015 percent, while\par the 3-year yield slid to 3.215 percent, its lowest\par since January 2014.\par     Still, interbank speculators sold the ringgit around the\par session's high of 3.7200 per dollar on concerns over possible\par cuts in sovereign rating, the debt issues of state-fund 1MDB and\par a slowing economy.\par     "Going forward, the MYR may weaken further due to the\par increasing risk of sovereign rating downgrade and liquidation\par of local government debt by foreign investors," said Heng Koon\par How, Credit Suisse Private Bank's senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist, in\par a client note.\par     The bank adjusted its three-month forecast for the ringgit\par to 3.8000 and 12-month forecast to 3.9500, he said.\par \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0530 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       122.71         122.70       -0.01\par   Sing dlr        1.3309         1.3337       +0.21\par   Taiwan dlr      30.734         31.062       +1.07\par   Korean won     1098.90        1107.10       +0.75\par   Baht             33.62          33.68       +0.16\par   Peso             45.02          45.11       +0.20\par   Rupiah        13300.00       13330.00       +0.23\par   Rupee            63.51          63.55       +0.07\par   Ringgit         3.7230         3.7445       +0.58\par  *Yuan            6.2095         6.2095       +0.00\par  \par   Change so far in 2015\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       122.71         119.66       -2.49\par   Sing dlr        1.3309         1.3260       -0.37\par   Taiwan dlr      30.734         31