\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Greece woes cause profit-taking from Fed-spurred weekly Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  gains\b0\par\par\uc2 822 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juni 2015\par 08:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Baht down; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Thai c.bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  "comfortable" with weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par     * Ringgit leads weekly Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, June 19 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  eased on Friday with anxiety over Greece's debt\par crisis increasing, but they were largely set to enjoy weekly\par gains on hopes the U.S. Federal Reserve may not raise interest\par rates in the near term.\par     The Thai baht slid after a senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par official told Reuters that \f28 \uc2 \f2 the Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  would be\par "comfortable" with a weaker \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for the export-dependent\par economy. \par     The Malaysian ringgit fell as traders took profits\par from the best-performing emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of the week.\par     The South Korean won earlier bucked the regional\par daily slide on sustained stop-loss dollar selling. The won pared\par gains as the yen turned weaker, increasing caution over\par possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par authorities to stem the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's strength.\par     Euro zone leaders will hold an emergency summit on Monday\par after their finance ministers failed to sign a deal on a\par cash-for-reforms agreement with Greece on Thursday.\par  \par     "Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  definitely bought time as the dollar may\par correct further after this week's FOMC," said Jeong My-young,\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Samsung\f28 \uc2 \f2  Futures' research head in Seoul, referring to the\par Federal Open Market Committee meeting.\par     "Still, markets have been underestimating problems in Europe\par and healthy U.S. data. So we may see more volatility in Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," Jeong said.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Wednesday signalled the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may\par raise interest rates more slowly than markets had expected.\par  Fixed income derivatives markets, including the\par Fed fund futures, expected the first rate hike only in\par December, even though many economists still saw a rise in\par September.\par     \par     RINGGIT, WON LEAD\par     Emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were poised to report weekly gains\par as the Fed's stance led investors to dump dollar holdings\par against regional units.\par     The ringgit has appreciated 1.0 percent against the dollar\par so far this week on stop-loss dollar selling, leading regional\par appreciation.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Negara Malaysia\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , on\par Thursday said the current ringgit's movements are affected by\par both global and domestic development. \par     "We think Negara, more than most AXJ central banks, is\par hoping the U.S. dollar rally is over," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tim Condon\f28 \uc2 \f2 ,\par economist with ING in a client note, referring to Asia ex-Japan.\par     Condon said the dollar rally is unlikely over yet and ING's\par year-end ringgit forecast versus the dollar is 3.85.\par     The ringgit hit a nine-year low of 3.7680 per dollar on June\par 8. Weak prices for commodities - a key export for Malaysia - and\par concerns for state-fund 1MDB's debt problems have hurt the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par     The won followed the Malaysian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  with a 0.9 percent\par appreciation so far this week on exporters' demand for\par settlements.\par     Singapore's dollar has gained 0.7 percent so far\par this week. The Indian rupee has risen 0.5 percent and\par the Taiwan dollar ended the week up 0.5 percent. The\par island's financial markets were closed on Friday.\par     The Philippine peso has appreciated 0.3 percent\par and the baht has risen 0.2 percent.\par     Emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are unlikely to maintain such\par upside momentum for the longer term as the Fed is still likely\par to raise interest rates later this year on solid U.S. economic\par data, analysts said.\par     "I still look to buy USD/Asia dip if we see EUR bounce on\par positive Greek news, etc.," said Jonathan Cavenagh, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strategist with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Westpac\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Singapore.\par     "We still feel U.S. data momentum is trending up."\par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0515 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       123.06         122.96       -0.08\par   Sing dlr        1.3349         1.3341       -0.06\par  *Taiwan dlr      31.062     