\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar's retreat supports Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 , Fed rate hike bets hurt May\b0\par\par\uc2 876 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Mai 2015\par 08:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Won leads Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  losses in May; worst month since Nov\par     * S.Korea warns of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem won's rise vs yen\par     * Baht down 2.3 pct in May, largest loss since Dec 2013\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SEOUL, May 29 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par edged up on Friday as the dollar took a breather from this\par week's rally, while regional units were set to post monthly\par losses in May on growing expectations for a U.S. interest rate\par hike this year.\par     South Korea's won failed to join Friday's rebound\par by Asian peers and suffered the worst month in six as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities warned of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb its rise\par against the yen. \par     The Taiwan dollar led regional appreciation,\par rising after foreign investors were net buyers of local stocks\par  in the previous three days. It pared some gains, as the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spotted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and there was demand for the\par U.S. dollar from importers.\par     The greenback fell against a basket of six major\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , with a decline versus the yen coming after\par Japanese Finance Minister Taro Aso said its recent drop had been\par "rough". \par     The dollar's retreat is seen as transitory and emerging\par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are likely to weaken further in June as the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  is expected to raise interest rates this year.\par     Contracts to buy previously-owned U.S. homes rose for a\par fourth consecutive month in April to a nine-year high, while\par initial claims for state jobless benefits stayed below 300,000,\par a threshold associated with a firming jobs market, for a 12th\par straight week. \par     "USD strength still has legs. It is still risk-off trades in\par Asia with high yielders underperforming," said Andy Ji, Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commonwealth Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2 , in\par Singapore, referring to higher-yielding \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  such as the\par Indonesian rupiah.\par     "U.S. economic data shows Q1 weakness was weather-related\par and the general view expressed by the Fed members still suggests\par a sooner than December hike is still on the cards."\par     Investors were awaiting revised data for the U.S.\par first-quarter economic growth due later in the day. A\par preliminary Reuters poll last week predicted that adjusted first\par quarter U.S. GDP numbers would be massively revised\par down and show a 0.7 percent contraction in the first three\par months of this year.\par     Sentiment towards most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  already\par worsened in the last two weeks, a Reuters poll showed on\par Thursday. \par         \par     YEN HURTS WON\par     Most regional units were on the course for monthly losses in\par May, led by the won. The South Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lost 3.2 percent\par against the dollar this month, the largest monthly depreciation\par since November, according to Thomson Reuters data.\par     The won came under pressure as the yen slumped to a near\par 13-year low against the dollar. That drove the won to\par a seven-year peak against the Japanese unit and spurred \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities.\par     South Korean exporters compete against Japanese rivals for\par key products such as cars.\par     The Malaysian ringgit followed the won, with a 2.6\par percent loss so far this month, as lower oil prices than in\par April underscored concerns that sliding crude may hurt the\par country's trade and fiscal account. Malaysia is a net oil\par exporter.\par     Thailand's baht has fallen 2.3 percent, which would\par be the largest monthly slide since December 2013. Foreign\par investors have been net sellers in local bond market so far in\par May.\par     Last month, \f28 \uc2 \f2 the Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  surprised markets by\par cutting its key policy rate and relaxing curbs on capital\par outflows.\par     The rupiah has eased 2.0 percent this month on corporate\par dollar demand and concerns over a slowing economy and current\par account deficit.\par     Singapore's dollar has lost 1.8 percent as the\par outlook for the city-state's economy stayed dark on uneven\par global growth.\par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0633 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       123.93         123.95       +0.02\par   Sing dlr        1.3482         1.3485       +0.02\par   Taiwan dlr      30.646         30.801    