\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  sentiment worsens on Fed policy bets, yuan an exception\b0\par\par\uc2 952 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Mai 2015\par 10:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Rupee short positions highest since August 2013\par     * Baht bearish bets largest since January 2014\par     * Won, rupiah short-positions at 2-month high\par     * Yuan long positions largest since late November\par \par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SEOUL, May 28 (Reuters) - Sentiment towards most emerging\par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  worsened in the last two weeks with short\par positions in India's rupee near a two-year high as expectations\par firmed that U.S. interest rates will move higher by year end, a\par Reuters poll showed on Thursday.\par     The Chinese yuan was an exception as its long\par positions hit a seven-month high, according to the survey of 20\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analysts at banks and fund managers conducted between\par Tuesday and Thursday.\par     Short positions in the rupee reached their largest\par since August 2013 as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell on expectations the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2  will deliver its third rate cut this year\par at next week's policy review, and on month-end corporate dollar\par demand.\par     Bearish bets on the won jumped to the highest\par since mid-March as the yen plunged to its lowest in\par almost 13 years against the dollar. That drove the won\par  to a seven-year peak against the Japanese unit and\par spurred \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par authorities.\par     The authorities have been spotted in efforts to curb the\par won's strength against the yen to relieve pressure on South\par Korean companies, which compete against Japanese rivals for key\par products such as cars.\par     Short positions in the rupiah also increased to the\par highest since mid-March on sustained corporate dollar demand.\par Persistent concerns over a slowdown in Southeast Asia's top\par economy and its chronic current account deficit were also\par factors boosting bearish bets on the rupiah.\par     Much of the pessimism against regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appears to\par have the U.S. Federal Reserve as a trigger. Fed Chair Janet\par Yellen last week said interest rates are likely to rise this\par year but the pace of tightening will depend on the strength of\par economic data.\par     A gauge of U.S. business investment spending plans rose\par solidly for a second straight month in April and consumer\par confidence perked up this month. New home sales rose last month.\par   \par     Thailand's baht suffered the largest short\par positions since January 2014 as foreign investors have been net\par sellers of local bonds so far this month.\par     Last month, \f28 \uc2 \f2 the Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  surprised markets by\par cutting its key policy rate and relaxed curbs on capital\par outflows. \par     Pessimistic bets on the Singapore dollar grew to\par the largest since early April amid an uncertain outlook for the\par city-state's economy due to uneven global growth. Industrial\par output in April fell 8.7 percent from a year earlier, its worst\par contraction since at least April 2013, data showed on Tuesday.\par  Consumer prices last month also posted their\par largest annual drop in five years. \par     The Malaysian ringgit's short positions rose as\par lower oil prices underscored concerns that low crude prices may\par hurt the country's trade and fiscal accounts. Malaysia is a net\par oil exporter.\par     \par     VIEWS TURN BEARISH ON TWD, PHP\par     Sentiment on the Taiwan dollar turned bearish as\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped up its efforts to limit further\par appreciation in the best-performing Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  so far this\par year. The authority asked major custodian banks to look into\par foreign customers' transactions, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official told\par Reuters on May 22. \par     Views on the Philippine peso also became\par pessimistic as growth in the first quarter unexpectedly slowed\par to a six-year low. \par     The yuan bucked the regional trend as Chinese policymakers\par signaled their keenness to keep the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stable. The\par renminbi hit a one-month high on May 22. \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  poll is focused on what analysts believe are\par the current market positions in nine Asian emerging market\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : the Chinese yuan, South Korean won, Singapore\par dollar, Indonesian rupiah, Taiwan dollar, Indian rupee,\par Philippine peso, Malaysian ringgit and the Thai baht.\par     The poll uses estimates of net long or short positions on a\par scale of minus 3 to plus 3. A score of plus 3 indicates the\par market is significantly long U.S. dollars.\par     The figures include positions held through non-deliverable\par forwards (NDFs).\par     The survey findings are provided below (positions\par in U.S. dollar versus each \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ):\par \par  DATE     CNY   KRW   SGD   IDR   TWD   INR   MYR   PHP   THB\par  28-May  -0.62  0.67  0.53  1.05  0.02  0.29  0.86  0.03  0.89\par  14-May  -0.45  0.11 -0.05  0.95 -0.30  0.22  0.41 -0.06  0.78\par  30-Apr  -0.48 -0.55 -0.44  0.43 -0.46 -0.18 -0.13 -0.12  0.33\par  16-Apr  -0.35  0.18  0.27  0.34  0.12 -0.59  1.08  0.02 -0.21\par  2-Apr   -0.13  0.14  0.69  0.74 -0.09 -0.51  1.09  0.13  0.14\par  19-Mar   0.46  1.10  1.48  1.33  0.53 -0.30  1.63  0.33  0.44\par  5-Mar    0.90  0.36  1.24  1.10  0.46 -0.64  1.34 -0.28  0.05\par  18-Feb   0.35  0.32  0.86  0.58  0.39 -0.15  0.74 -0.17 -0.15\par  5-Feb    0.62  0.04  1.16  0.35  0.36 -0.62  1.42 -0.35  0.10\par  22-Jan  -0.04  0.02  0.72  0.38  0.19 -0.73  1.69 -0.02  0.03\par  \par  (Additional reporting by Shaloo Shrivastava in BENGALURU and\par Suvashree Dey Choudhury in MUMBAI; Editing by Shri Navaratnam)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-5-28T09:34:27.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150528eb5s00bfa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
