\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Fed rate hike bets hurt Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 ; won, rupiah hit two-month lows\b0\par\par\uc2 846 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Mai 2015\par 07:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Won falls as yen's 8-year low raises \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  caution\par     * Rupiah down on importers; c.bank limits downside\par     * Ringgit hits 1-month low, 3.6558/dollar eyed\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SEOUL, May 27 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par slipped on Wednesday as solid U.S. economic data boosted\par expectations the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  will raise interest rates this\par year and undermined the appeal of the region's higher yields.\par     The won hit a near two-month low as the yen's\par  slide to an eight-year low increased caution over\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par authorities to stem its strength against the Japanese unit.\par     Indonesia's rupiah touched its weakest in more than\par two months on month-end dollar demand from importers.\par     The Malaysian ringgit fell to a near one-month low\par as overnight losses in oil prices rekindled concerns that low\par crude prices may hurt the country's trade and fiscal account.\par Malaysia is a net oil exporter.\par     The U.S. dollar rose to a one-month high against a\par basket of six major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  with the yen below 123 per\par greenback, its weakest since July 2007.\par     That came after a gauge of U.S. business investment spending\par plans rose solidly for a second straight month in April and\par consumer confidence perked up this month. New home sales rose\par last month. \par     "Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will fall further," said Yuna Park, a\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and bond analyst at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dongbu Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Seoul, adding\par regional outperformers including the won may suffer more than\par others as investors may book profits from them.\par     "Strong U.S. data, especially after Yellen's hawkish\par comments, raised the case of a U.S. rate increase," she said.\par "The hike may happen in September, but markets will prepare in\par advance."\par     Fed Chair \f28 \uc2 \f2 Janet Yellen\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Friday said interest rates are\par likely to rise this year but the pace of tightening will depend\par on the strength of economic data.\par     \par     WON\par     The won lost as much as 0.8 percent to 1,109.3 per dollar,\par its weakest since March 31.\par     Caution increased over possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South\par Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities to prevent the won from\par further outperforming the yen.\par     The South Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has eased 0.8 percent against the\par dollar so far this year, while the yen has lost 2.8 percent,\par according to Thomson Reuters data.\par     South Korea's companies competed against Japan's rivals for\par key products such as cars.\par     The won pared some earlier losses as local exporters bought\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on dips for month-end settlements.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has a chart support at 1,109.9, the 61.8\par percent Fibonacci retracement of its appreciation from March to\par April, analysts said.\par     \par     RUPIAH\par     The rupiah eased 0.2 percent to 13,236 per dollar, its\par lowest level since March 17, tracking its weakness in overnight\par non-deliverable forwards markets.\par     The official Jakarta Interbank Spot Dollar Rate,\par which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  introduced in 2013 to manage exchange\par rate fluctuations, was fixed at 13,229 rupiah per dollar, weaker\par than the previous 13,192.\par     Spot rupiah pared some of the losses as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was\par spotted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  around the session low to support the\par worst-performing Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  so far this year, traders said.\par     \par     RINGGIT\par     The ringgit slid 0.4 percent to 3.6430 per dollar, its\par weakest since April 21, as dollar demand linked to daily fixing\par added pressure.\par     The Malaysian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may weaken to 3.6558, the 61.8\par percent retracement level of its appreciation from March to\par April as it cleared a chart support area around 3.6330, analysts\par said.\par     It has the 38.2 percent level at 3.6333 and a 55-day moving\par average at 3.6338. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had been firmer than the average\par since late April.\par \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0525 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       122.97         123.10       +0.11\par   Sing dlr        1.3488   