\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Taiwan dlr leads Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  gains despite c.bank step; Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  down for week\b0\par\par\uc2 865 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Mai 2015\par 07:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Taiwan c.bank says to monitor foreign inflows\par     * Taiwan dollar strongest since Nov. 3\par     * Rupiah down despite \f28 \uc2 \f2 S&P\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Indonesia outlook upgrade\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, May 22 (Reuters) - Inflows into stocks helped the\par Taiwan dollar to its strongest in more than six months on\par Friday, prompting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to dampen its rise as it led\par gains among emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  following disappointing\par U.S. economic data.\par      Most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , however, were on the course\par for weekly losses with the Indonesian rupiah down even\par after \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Thursday raised its outlook on the\par country's sovereign rating. \par     South Korea's won gained as exporters chased it\par for settlements before a long weekend. The country's financial\par markets will be closed on Monday.\par     The Malaysian ringgit advanced as a rebound in oil\par prices eased concerns that lower crude may hurt the country's\par trade and fiscal accounts. Malaysia is a net oil exporter.\par     Singapore's dollar found chart support around\par 1.3400 per the U.S. dollar, prompting short covering in a\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that has been worst performer in emerging Asia this\par week.\par     The U.S. dollar fell against a basket of six major\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as home sales fell in April, and the strength of the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hurt manufacturing activity in May, although the labour\par market continued to tighten. But, the dollar\par index had risen more than 2 percent for the week, and some\par analysts saw emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  staying under pressure.\par     "We do continue to expect the Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  block to\par weaken," said Heng Koon How, Credit Suisse Private Bank's senior\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist. "We see initial signs of re-acceleration of\par US growth in Q2, with improving labour market gains. Our base\par case remains that of a first Fed rate hike in September and\par continued USD strength."\par     Investors also stayed cautious ahead of Fed Chair Janet\par Yellen's speech on the U.S. economic outlook before the Greater\par Providence Chamber of Commerce Economic Outlook Luncheon at 1700\par GMT.    \par     \par     TAIWAN C.BANK\par     The Taiwan dollar rose 0.8 percent to 30.405 per\par U.S. dollar, its strongest since Nov. 3. Local shares \par advanced 0.7 percent.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  asked major custodian banks to look\par into foreign customers' transactions, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official\par told Reuters, amid worries that Asia's best performing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par of the year too far could appreciate too much. \par     The island's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has risen 0.7 percent against the\par greenback so far this week, defying regional depreciation,\par according to Thomson Reuters data.\par     Among regional losers, the rupiah has lost 0.4 percent\par against the U.S. dollar so far this week on dollar demand from\par Indonesian importers and concerns over a current account\par deficit.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 S&P\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Thursday raised its outlook on Indonesia's\par speculative-grade sovereign rating to positive from stable, in\par regconition of the government's improved policies. But, the move\par failed to encourage traders to cut bearish bets on the rupiah.\par     "The current account deficit will be higher in the next\par quarters because of infrastructure projects and potential higher\par imports ahead of Eid al-Fitr," said a Jakarta-based \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par trader, referring to the end of the fasting month of Ramadan.\par     The holidays fall in mid-July this year.\par     The Singapore dollar has fallen 0.7 percent so far this\par week, underperforming regional peers, after gains in the\par previous five consecutive weeks. The ringgit has also eased 0.7\par percent.\par     The won has fallen 0.4 percent for the week as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities were spotted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem\par its appreciation.\par     Thailand's baht, however, bucked the regional\par trend, to gain 0.5 percent gain on inflows to stocks and bonds\par as some investors expected the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cut interest rates\par further.\par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0515 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       120.76         121.02       