\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Financial Services News of the Day\b0\par\par\uc2 584 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 2015\par 16:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FINANCIAL SERVICES TOP STORIES \par  \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 GE\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO EXIT THE BULK OF \f28 \uc2 \f2 GE CAPITAL\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 GE\f28 \uc2 \f2  has resolved to part ways with the bulk of \f28 \uc2 \f2 GE Capital\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the giant finance business that long accounted for around half the company's profits but whose risks have rattled investors and weighed on its stock. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FIXED INCOME HEDGE FUNDS WRESTLE WITH QE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 One month into the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's massive bond-buying program, fixed income hedge fund managers are trying to get their heads round how to trade it. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DEUTSCHE BANK\f28 \uc2 \f2  CLOSE TO RESOLVING INTEREST-RATE PROBE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  is said to be close to resolving a long-running investigation into the manipulation of interest rates, but demands from New York's financial regulator are pushing the penalty to new heights. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA FINALLY GETS CHEAPER CREDIT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Lots of things are getting cheaper in China, and credit is finally one of them. Through a combination of rate cuts and a tiny bump in inflation since January, China's real benchmark lending rate has edged down to 4.35%. \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SOUTH KOREA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  DENIES \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean officials denied the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury Department\f28 \uc2 \f2 's fresh report on Seoul's suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 GF SECURITIES\f28 \uc2 \f2  JUMPS 40% IN DEBUT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's fourth-largest brokerage by assets \f28 \uc2 \f2 GF Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  jumped 40% in its trading debut in Hong Kong, after raising $3.6 billion in Asia's largest initial public offering this year. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 FEDERAL RESERVE\f28 \uc2 \f2  FINALIZES RULE TO EASE SMALL BANK MERGERS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  finalized a rule that will allow more small banks to exceed debt limits when financing mergers and acquisitions, implementing a law Congress passed in December. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BATS SAYS SOME STOCKS SHOULDN'T TRADE ON ITS EXCHANGES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The new CEO and president of BATS said the company was planning to file a new proposal to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 SEC\f28 \uc2 \f2  that would require thinly-traded stocks to trade only at the exchange where they are publicly listed. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CITIGROUP\f28 \uc2 \f2  HEAD OF RISK \f28 \uc2 \f2 BRIAN LEACH\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO RETIRE--MEMO \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brian Leach\f28 \uc2 \f2 , head of franchise risk and strategy at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citigroup\f28 \uc2 \f2 , is retiring, according to memos from Mr. Leach and Citigroup Chief Executive \f28 \uc2 \f2 Michael Corbat\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HEDGE FUND KAMUNTING STREET CAPITAL SHUTTING DOWN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A former \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citigroup\f28 \uc2 \f2  trading star is shutting down his hedge fund partly because of losses related to oil's historic plunge, the latest Wall Street shakeout in the aftermath of a dramatic decline in crude prices. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CANADA'S SCOTIABANK CONSIDERS CUBA EXPANSION \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Nova Scotia\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Canada's third-largest bank by assets, is exploring potential expansion opportunities in Cuba now that the U.S. is moving to normalize relations with the Caribbean country, the lender's top executive said. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JEFFERIES TO SELL BACHE FUTURES UNIT, BUY \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  OPS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Jefferies Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  has agreed to sell its Bache commodities and financial derivatives unit to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Soci\u233\'00\'E9t\u233\'00\'E9 G\u233\'00\'E9n\u233\'00\'E9rale\f28 \uc2 \f2 , while bulking up in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by buying Faros Trading, a unit of FXCM. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 GOLDMAN SACHS\f28 \uc2 \f2  MAKES SECOND SENIOR \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  HIRE FROM \f28 \uc2 \f2 J.P. MORGAN\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 J.P. Morgan Chase\f28 \uc2 \f2 's James Ellery, who left his position as global head of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  options at the firm in March, is to join \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2 , according to two people familiar with the matter. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FRENCH MAGISTRATES OPEN CRIMINAL INVESTIGATION OF \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  said it has been placed under formal criminal investigation by French magistrates over the conduct of \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Swiss private bank in 2006 and 2007 for alleged tax-related offenses.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 April 10, 2015 10:00 ET (14:00 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150410eb4a0022m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
