\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For April 10\b0\par\par\uc2 740 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 2015\par 08:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0600 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA'S CONSUMER INFLATION INCHES UP IN MARCH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China posted another modest rise in consumer inflation in March, giving policy makers room for more aggressive stimulus for a sluggish economy. (published 0318 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN SAYS IT IS PURSUING BALANCED FISCAL, MONETARY POLICIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In the face of fresh U.S. criticism that Japan is too reliant on monetary policy and too hasty to rebuild its finances, the nation's finance minister responded Friday by saying that Tokyo is pursuing a balanced approach to growth and budgetary challenges. (published 0024 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MODI ARRIVES IN FRANCE FOR BOAT TRIP ON THE SEINE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indian Prime Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Narendra Modi\f28 \uc2 \f2  arrived in Paris on Thursday evening on the start of his three-nation tour that includes a visit to Germany and Canada. (published 0516 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA ECONOMY IN 'TARGETED RANGE,' NO DEFLATION SEEN - ECONOMIST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's economy has been facing downward pressure but hasn't slipped out of its targeted growth range, a senior economist said Friday. (published 0504 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MALAYSIA FEBRUARY INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION RISES 5.2% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's industrial production climbed 5.2% in February from a year earlier, slightly above market expectations, thanks to strong gains in mining output, official data Friday showed. (published 0400 GMT) \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SOUTH KOREA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  DENIES \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKETS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean officials Friday denied the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury Department\f28 \uc2 \f2 's fresh report on Seoul's suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets. (published 0248 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIAN HOUSING FINANCE INVESTMENT SLOWS IN FEBRUARY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The value of lending to Australian property investors slowed sharply in February easing concerns about overheating in the housing market. (published 0156 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINES JANUARY NET FOREIGN DIRECT INVESTMENT $263 MLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Foreign direct investments in the Philippines showed a net inflow of $263 million in January, helped mainly by funds placed by foreign companies in debt securities issued by their local affiliates, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Friday. (published 0552 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 GF SECURITIES\f28 \uc2 \f2  JUMPS 40% IN TRADING DEBUT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's fourth-largest brokerage by assets \f28 \uc2 \f2 GF Securities Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . jumped 40% in its trading debut in Hong Kong Friday, after raising US$3.6 billion in Asia's largest initial public offering this year. (published 0159 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NOBLE REJECTS MUDDY WATERS' CRITICISMS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Commodities trader Noble Group said it categorically rejects accusations leveled at it by short seller Muddy Waters, in a lengthy response filed early Friday to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Singapore Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (published 0102 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par LG SEEKS FEEDBACK AHEAD OF G4 LAUNCH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In what appears to be an attempt at creating more buzz for its new flagship smartphone, \f28 \uc2 \f2 LG Electronics\f28 \uc2 \f2  said it will allow select customers to test drive its G4. (published 0343 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PEACE MAP HOLDING TO RAISE HK$313.5 MILLION VIA SHARE PLACEMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Peace Map Holding Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., which provides geographic information to businesses in China and is engaged in the mining and exploration of mineral resources in Mongolia, said Friday it is seeking to raise HK$313.5 million from a share placement and will use the net proceeds for general working capital. (published 0041 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SINGTEL REJIGS SENIOR MANAGEMENT, NAMES NEW CHIEF FINANCIAL OFFICER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore Telecommunications Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Friday announced several senior management changes, including promoting deputy chief financial officer to group chief financial officer. (published 0246 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINO CONSTRUCTION\f28 \uc2 \f2  SAYS NOT AWARE OF ANY REASON TO EXPLAIN PRICE SURGE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sino Construction Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Friday says it is not aware of any reason or information that could explain a surge in the company's share price. (published 0343 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SINGAPORE'S SMRT FORMS MAINTENANCE VENTURE WITH \f28 \uc2 \f2 FAIVELEY TRANSPORT\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SMRT Corp. Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (S53.SG) has formed a maintenance joint venture with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Faiveley Transport SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  (LEY.FR). (published 0250 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ASIAN SHARES MOSTLY HIGHER; NIKKEI TOUCHES 20000 -- 2ND UPDATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tokyo stocks briefly broke above 20000 for the first time in 15 years in early Friday trading, the latest milestone in the market's bull run, while stocks in Hong Kong extended a six-session winning streak. (published 0246 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 COMMODITIES: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OIL FUTURES STABLE AFTER VOLATILE WEEK, WTI ABOVE $50/BBL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude-oil futures were mostly stable in Asian trade Friday after a week of high volatility, with U.S. oil prices holding up at the $50 a barrel mark. (published 0531 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 April 10, 2015 02:02 ET (06:02 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150410eb4a000hk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
