\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  up after Yellen, China PMI; rupiah hovers near 17-year low\b0\par\par\uc2 807 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 2015\par 06:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Rupiah firms; month-end corporate dollar bids limits gains\par     * Won up more than 1 pct on exporters, stop-loss dlr selling\par     * Taiwan dollar rises on exporters, stock inflows\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, Feb 25 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par rose on Wednesday after Federal Reserve Chair \f28 \uc2 \f2 Janet Yellen\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par suggested the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will not rush into raising\par interest rates, while Indonesia's rupiah hovered near 17-year\par lows.\par     Regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gained as better-than-expected Chinese\par manufacturing activity eased some concerns over a slowdown in\par the world's second-largest economy.\par     The South Korean won and the Taiwan dollar\par  advanced on exporter demand for month-end settlements.\par Malaysia's ringgit gained on short-covering.\par     Yellen said before the U.S. Senate Banking Committee on\par Tuesday that any modification of the Fed's forward guidance\par should not be read as an indication of interest rate hikes in a\par couple of meetings. \par     The comments defied expectations that she would provide a\par more specific time frame to revive prospects for higher U.S.\par borrowing costs as early as mid-year. Such expectations hurt\par most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  earlier this week.\par     Adding to support for regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the flash\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2 /Markit Purchasing Managers' Index (PMI) for China inched up\par to a four-month high of 50.1 in February, beating market\par expectations. \par     "Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could see some slight positives for a short term on\par the back of dollar reprieve from Yellen's comments and commodity\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could see some upmove from the positive \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  flash\par PMI," said Saktiandi Supaat, head of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  research for Maybank in\par Singapore.\par     Still, he had doubts about appreciation in the long term,\par saying "the dollar will continue to mildly go up ahead of the\par next FOMC."\par     The Chinese yuan failed to join the regional\par appreciation trend as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fixed its daily mid-point\par weaker on the first trading day after the week-long Lunar New\par Year holidays. \par     \par     RUPIAH\par     The rupiah started the day up 0.4 percent at a\par session high of 12,850 per dollar, tracking gains in regional\par peers, before retreating.\par     Foreign ownership of rupiah-denominated bonds rose to a\par record high in nominal terms this week, the finance ministry\par said. \par     The Indonesian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gave up most of its earlier gains on\par increasing dollar demand from local companies for month-end\par payments.\par     The official Jakarta Interbank Spot Dollar Rate,\par which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  introduced in 2013 to manage exchange\par rate fluctuations, was fixed at 12,887 rupiah per dollar, weaker\par than the previous session's 12,866.\par     On Tuesday, the rupiah fell to 12,897 per dollar, the\par weakest since Dec. 16 when it hit 12,930, the lowest since\par August 1998.\par     \par     WON\par     The won rose more than 1 percent as demand from exporters\par caused traders to dump dollar holdings to stop losses.\par     Traders had added long dollar positions earlier as importers\par bought the greenback and amid caution over possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities to curb the won's\par strength.\par     \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\par     The Taiwan dollar gained as sustained stock inflows lifted\par local shares.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was spotted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to limit the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's upside, traders said.\par     Foreign investors bought a combined net T$73.1 billion ($2.3\par billion) worth of shares in February by Tuesday, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Taiwan Stock\par Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2  data showed. They were net buyers in the stock market\par in all trading days this month, the data showed. \par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0510 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       118.67         118.98       +0.26\par   Sing dlr        1.3568         1.3573       +0.04\par   Taiwan dlr      31.472         31.688       +0.69\par   Korean won     1100.00        1109.90       +0.90\par   Baht             32.56          32.57       +0.05\par   Peso             44.16          44.34       +0.40\par   Rupiah        12880.00       12895.00       +0.12\par   Rupee            62.06          62.20