\par\par \b \uc2 INTERVIEW-S.Korea  \highlight22\uc2 fx \highlight\uc2  rate seen market determined in recent months -\uc2 IMF\b0\par\par\uc2 377 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 2015\par 06:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, Feb 13 (Reuters) - The \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 , which has previously urged \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  against \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, says the won has moved in line with market trends in the past six months, suggesting authorities refrained from forceful \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Recent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data shows \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves have inched down over several months, a sign that authorities in the export-reliant economy have veered away from the aggressive dollar buying of the past when the won rose sharply.\par \par \uc2 "From the data that are available, the exchange rate has been market-determined for the last six months I think, so the government is pursuing their policy of exchange rate flexibility at the moment. We think that's the right thing to do," said IMF division chief Brian Aitken in an interview with Reuters.\par \par \uc2 South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities are known to step into the market in times of volatility, usually to weaken the won against the dollar in order to support exporters, according to traders and analysts.\par \par \uc2 That has sparked complaints from the United States and \uc2 IMF\uc2  in the past, with the \uc2 IMF\uc2 's report last year saying there is no need for further accumulation of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Local policymakers in recent months have said that although they engage in smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lessen fluctuations, they refrain from fighting against the tide.\par \par \uc2 While the won reached five-year highs last year, the dollar began strengthening dramatically in November, pressuring the won and other Asian currecies.\par \par \uc2 Aitken also said South Korea's household debt burden does not pose an imminent threat to the financial sector.\par \par \uc2 "One of the very interesting things about Korean households too, is that while debt is rising as share of income, so are assets. So they're not borrowing to spend," he said.\par \par \uc2 Earlier on Friday, data showed South Korean households' disposable income growth picked up in the October-December quarter from the previous quarter, brightening prospects for private consumption.\par \par \uc2 Aitken's comments came during the \uc2 IMF\uc2 's yearly visit to South Korea to discuss economic developments and policies. (Reporting by Christine Kim; Editing by Tony Munroe and Simon Cameron-Moore)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-2-16T05:00:05.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150213eb2d006va\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
