\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-S.Korea economy faces risks from global uncertainties, oil to help -\uc2 IMF\b0\par\par\uc2 447 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 2015\par 08:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 * S.Korea 2015 outlook faces uncertainties               \par \par \uc2 * S.Korea to benefit from low oil prices               \par \par \uc2 * Won has moved in line with other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently   (Adds more \uc2 IMF\uc2  comments from press conference)               \par \par \uc2 By Christine Kim               \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, Feb 13 (Reuters) - The South Korean economy faces uncertainties this year due to global weakness, the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  said on Friday, but expects it will benefit from low oil prices and doesn't see  an imminent risk from rising household debt.               \par \par \uc2 Given the backdrop of an improving U.S. economy and ongoing concerns over the outlook for China, Japan and the E.U., South Korea faces a risk that a "self-reinforcing downside dynamic" of weak growth and inflation could take hold, the \uc2 IMF\uc2  said.               \par \par \uc2 However, Asia's fourth-largest economy is better placed  compared to other emerging economies, it said.               \par \par \uc2 "Weakness in the global economy is the biggest risk but South Korea is in a very good position to (withstand) that weakness. Korea is well-placed to face any kind of shocks that may be coming," said Kalpana Kochhar, deputy director of the Asia and Pacific Department at the \uc2 IMF\uc2 .               \par \par \uc2 South Korea has enhanced external buffers that would help limit the impact of any renewed global financial volatility, the mission said, while South Korea's household debt does not pose a financial or systemic risk because debt and assets are both rising.               \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 IMF\uc2  also noted that South Korea has monetary and fiscal policy space to respond if needed, although it advised the government to take timely action should the situation warrant it. The mission also recommended far-reaching reforms to underpin long-run growth.               \par \par \uc2 Kochhar said it is too early to assess whether South Korea's economic weakness will persist or whether it has already bottomed out.               \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 IMF\uc2 , which has previously urged \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  against \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, also said the won has moved in line with market trends in the past six months, suggesting authorities refrain from forceful \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .               \par \par \uc2 Recent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data shows \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves have inched down over several months, a sign that authorities in the export-reliant economy have veered away from the aggressive dollar buying of the past when the won rose sharply.               \par \par \uc2 "From the data that are available, the exchange rate has been market-determined for the last six months I think, so the government is pursuing their policy of exchange rate flexibility at the moment. We think that's the right thing to do," said IMF division chief Brian Aitken in an interview with Reuters earlier this week.               \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-2-13T08:13:59.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150213eb2d009kp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
