\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won leads Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  losses as yen nears 120\b0\par\par\uc2 725 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Dezember 2014\par 06:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * S.Korea \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  caution up as won at 6-yr high vs yen\par     * Rupiah at 6-year low, JISDOR record low\par     * Indonesia c.bank spotted around 12,320/dlr-traders\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, Dec 4 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par slid on Thursday as the dollar stayed at multi-year highs\par against major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on solid U.S. jobs data and ahead of an\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy meeting later in the day.\par     South Korea's won underperformed regional peers\par as the yen plumbed seven-year lows against the dollar,\par heading towards the 120 per dollar level.\par     The Indonesian rupiah hit a six-year low on dollar\par demand from local corporates. The country's second biggest party\par on Wednesday re-elected tycoon Aburizal Bakrie as its chief for\par the next five years, dimming hopes that the opposition party\par would join President Joko Widodo's minority coalition.\par     \par     The dollar index, the greenback's performance against\par six major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , hovered around its highest since March\par 2009.\par     U.S. private companies added workers at a fairly brisk pace\par in November and the service sector expanded strongly, indicating\par the world's top economy holds growth momentum. \par     By contrast, the euro zone economy may be on the verge of\par another contraction, prompting some expectations that the ECB\par may be preparing to add more stimulus, although a full-blown\par quantitative easing programme is seen as unlikely at the policy\par review later in the day.\par     "If the ECB signals another easing, the dollar will gain\par momentum further and Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will weaken," said Yuna Park, a\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and bond analyst at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dongbu Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Seoul.\par     "A less dovish ECB may help the euro rebound and Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may follow that, but that would be only temporary."\par     \par     WON\par     The won slid against the dollar on caution that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South\par Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities may \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to check\par their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's strength against the yen.\par     The won hit 9.2872 to the Japanese unit, its strongest since\par August 2008. Two countries compete in exports markets for\par various products such as cars.\par     The won has a chart resistance area between 9.2000-9.3000,\par levels struck July and August 2008 during the early stages of\par the global financial crisis, analysts said.\par     \par     RUPIAH\par     The rupiah eased 0.2 percent to 12,319 per dollar, its\par weakest since November 2008. \par     The official Jakarta Interbank Spot Dollar Rate (JISDOR),\par which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  introduced last year in an effort to\par manage exchange rate fluctuations, was fixed at 12,318 rupiah\par per dollar, the weakest since the launch.\par     Foreign banks sold the rupiah, and most government bond\par prices fell.\par     The rupiah, however, pared some of its earlier losses as the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was spotted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  around 12,320 via state-run\par banks to limit the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's decline, traders said.\par     "It is possible to test 12,350 in a near term, but the\par 12,320 is capped for now with unlimited offers there," said a\par Jakarta-based \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader, referring to dollar selling by\par state-run banks.\par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0435 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       119.93         119.79       -0.12\par   Sing dlr        1.3142         1.3122       -0.15\par   Taiwan dlr      31.139         31.167       +0.09\par   Korean won     1116.80        1112.90       -0.35\par   Baht             32.89          32.86       -0.08\par   Peso             44.67          44.68       +0.02\par   Rupiah        12315.00       12297.00       -0.15\par   Rupee            61.91          61.91       -0.01\par   Ringgit         3.4470         3.4435       -0.10\par   Yuan            6.1498         6.1500       +0.00\par  \par   Change so far in 2014\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       119.93         105.28      -12.22\par   Sing dlr        1.3142         1.2632       -3.88\par   Taiwan dlr      31.139         29.950       -3.82\par   Korean won     1116.80        1055.40       -5.50\par   Baht             32.89          32.86       -0.08\par   Peso             44.67          44.40       -0.62\par   Rupiah      