\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Philippine peso weaker after disappointing GDP, Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  up\b0\par\par\uc2 652 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 November 2014\par 05:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Philippine Q3 growth slows to over 5-years\par     * Won leads Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains; S.Korea \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  suspected\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, Nov 27 (Reuters) - The Philippine peso fell on\par Thursday after the economy weakened to its slowest pace in more\par than five years in the third quarter, while most emerging Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose after soft U.S. data pushed down \f28 \uc2 \f2 Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  yields\par and hurt the dollar.\par     The peso eased 0.1 percent to 44.96 per dollar,\par turning weaker after data showed the Philippine economy expanded\par a seasonally adjusted 0.4 percent in the July-September period\par from the previous quarter. Manila shares \par lost 0.8 percent, underperforming regional equity markets.\par     Third-quarter growth was the weakest since the first quarter\par of 2009 and came in well below expectations of 1.4 percent\par growth in a Reuters poll.\par     Economic planning Secretary \f28 \uc2 \f2 Arsenio Balisacan\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a\par media briefing it would be a "big challenge" to hit the low end\par of the 2014 growth target of 6.5 to 7.5 percent. \par     The dismal data boosted expectations that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par will hold rates for an extended period before resuming its\par tightening cycle. \par     "It's a case for them not to do anything at this point,"\par said Patrick Ella, economist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Security Bank Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Manila,\par referring to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas\f28 \uc2 \f2 .  "This figure gives\par them a case to pause... a longer pause past Q1."\par     \par     WON\par     South Korea's won rose as much as 0.6 percent to\par 1,100.3 per dollar, its strongest since Nov. 19, on increasing\par demand from exporters for month-end settlements.\par     Data showed the nation's current account surplus in October\par rose to a seasonally adjusted $7.32 billion from a revised $4.99\par billion surplus in September as imports fell. \par     The dollar eased against the yen and euro as\par U.S. data on consumers, housing and manufacturing pushed the\par benchmark 10-year \f28 \uc2 \f2 Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  note yield to a one-month\par low on Wednesday. \par     The won, however, pared some of its earlier gains with \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South\par Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities suspected of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par check its strength against the yen.\par     Earlier, the won advanced to 9.3552 against the Japanese\par unit, its strongest since August 2008.\par     \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\par     The Taiwan dollar rose from Wednesday's close,\par after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to check gains in the previous\par session, according to traders.\par     The island's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tracked gains in the won and yen,\par though oil importers bought U.S. dollars for payments and \par limited the Taiwan dollar's upside, traders said.\par \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0410 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     