\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Subdued by Lukewarm U.S. Data -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,769 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 November 2014\par 01:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.1316-6.1396    6.1235-6.1500 \par USD/TWD   30.860-31.000    30.690-31.200 \par USD/KRW    1,100-1,1109     1,095-1,110 \par USD/SGD   1.2952-1.3000    1.2950-1.3056 \par USD/MYR   3.3410-3.3570    3.3250-3.3730 \par USD/THB    32.70-32.76      32.50-32.89 \par USD/PHP    44.91-44.94      44.82-45.07 \par USD/IDR   12,120-12,190    12,080-12,230 \par USD/INR    61.61-61.82      61.42-62.00 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--uptrend. The overnight slippage of the U.S. dollar index might weigh on spot USD/CNY - which is still in a technical uptrend - via a lower daily benchmark rate. If the dollar were to end the day below 6.1316 and thus out of the Bollinger uptrend channel and also below the Ichimoku Cloud support, there could be USD/CNY weakness - thereby yuan strength - ahead. There may be a shift in sentiment toward the yuan after the government unexpectedly cut its 1-year lending rate recently - signalling its concern for economic growth. China releases industrial profit data for October at 0130 GMT. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/CNY is at 6.1316 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud and base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 6.1235 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is at 6.1396 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 6.1477 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance), before 6.1500 (round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--uptrend. The USD/TWD daily Bollinger uptrend channel could be threatened by overnight U.S. dollar weakness due to lukewarm U.S. economic data. The pair could break the 30.860 base of the channel and head for the 20-day Bollinger mid support line at 30.690. A Thursday close below 30.860 would nullify the bullish technical bias for USD/TWD. The price of the 1-month USD/TWD nondeliverable forward contract in the offshore market may fall back under that of the spot contract if speculative demand for the dollar erodes due to data Wednesday suggesting that the U.S. economic recovery is still anemic. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.860 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 30.690 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 30.500 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 31.000 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 31.030 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 31.200 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--consolidation lower. USD/KRW has fallen out of the Bollinger uptrend channel and could soon test the round-figure trading barrier at 1,100 - a break of which could trigger stoploss orders that might weigh the greenback further. USD/KRW might find a stronger support at 1,095 where the 20-day Bollinger mid support line awaits. But as the won rallies versus the U.S. dollar, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cannot be ruled out. The South Korea won is still close to its strongest versus the yen since 2008, a factor that could influence \uc2 the Bank of Korea\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the USD/KRW spot market to weaken the won. A stronger won versus the yen makes South Korea exports' less competitively-priced versus those of Japan. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,100 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 1,095 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 1,090 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is at 1,109 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1,110 (round-figure trading barrier), before 1,120 (round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--consolidation lower. USD/SGD has lost its bullish technical bias due to Wednesday's bearish closing. The pair is now likely to slip toward the 20-day Bollinger mid support line at 1.2952. Data released in the U.S. on Wednesday depressed the U.S. dollar. A higher than expected number of jobless claims, weaker new home sales, and tepid inflation were factors that weighed on the greenback. Singapore's industrial output for October rose 0.2% on-year, sharply lower than forecasts for a rise of 2.1%. The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was however unaffected by the data and continues to be guided by external factors instead. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2952 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 1.2950 (psychological support), before 1.2900 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1.3000 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 1.3004 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1.3056 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--consolidation lower. USD/MYR could test the 20-day Bollinger mid support at 3.3410 as the greenback slipped again overnight following poorer-than-expected U.S. economic data. A confirmed break of the 20-day Bollinger mid line could lead to the entrance of the daily Bollinger downtrend channel at 3.3250. Fundamentally, the reduced likelihood of earlier-than-forecast U.S. interest rate hikes and the Malaysian government's announcement of a cut in fuel subsidies - a positive for the budget deficit - are bearish factors for USD/MYR. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.3410 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 3.3345 (monthly Ichimoku Cloud support), before 3.3250 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 3.3570 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.3730 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.4000 (round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--consolidation lower. USD/THB may enter the daily Bollinger downtrend channel at 32.70 as the U.S. dollar softens due to lackluster economic data released Wednesday. The activation of the downtrend channel - contingent on a Thursday close below 32.70 - would suggest the baht rallies versus the U.S. dollar in the near term. The intermediate downside target for USD/THB would be the daily Ichimoku Cloud support zone at 32.40. The baht may also find strength from Thailand's strongest export data in 21 months. Data released Wednesday revealed a nearly 4.0% rise in exports in October - especially encouraging because gains were seen in various sectors including automotive, electronics, and agriculture. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 32.70 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 32.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 32.76 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), then at 32.83 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 32.89 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--possible downtrend. USD/PHP is likely to break the October trendline at 44.91 which could give way to the Bollinger downtrend channel that begins at 44.88. A confirmation of the downtrend channel coming into play - contingent on a Thursday close below 44.88 - would weigh the dollar. The market maybe capitulating on long-USD positions as U.S. economic data released overnight failed to meet expectations. A possible catalyst for peso strength could be the Philippines' third-quarter gross domestic product data due at 0200 GMT. Upbeat trade figures released Tuesday bode well for the GDP report. Analysts forecast the economy grew 6.5% on-year in the third quarter versus the 6.4% growth in the second quarter. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 44.91 (October trendline support), then at 44.88 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 44.82 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 44.94 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), then at 45.00 (round-figure trading barrier and daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 45.07 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--consolidation lower. USD/IDR may subside lower within its consolidation range of 12,120-12,190 but is unlikely to break the daily Ichimoku Cloud support at 12,080 due to thin trading volumes expected ahead of the U.S. market holiday Thursday. The U.S. dollar slipped again overnight after a poorer-than-expected batch of economic data released Wednesday. The rise of weekly unemployment claims and the lukewarm U.S. inflation readings may have persuaded punters to take profit on long-USD positions. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 12,120 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 12,080 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support and base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 12,000 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is at 12,190 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 12,230 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--uptrend nullified. USD/INR is likely to slip toward the 20-day Bollinger mid support line at 61.61 after having lost its bullish bias Wednesday. The dollar closed below the 61.81 base of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel - suggesting to chart-savvy traders that the rally may be over for now. This could motivate profit-taking of long-USD positions in the near term. If USD/INR breaks the October trendline support at 61.60, there could be more downside to come. Overnight greenback weakness stemming from below-forecast U.S. economic data is broadly weighing on USD/Asia Thursday. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 61.61 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 61.60 (October trendline support), before 61.42 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 61.82 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel, then at 62.00 (round-figure trading barrier and top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 62.22 (9-month high).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 26 Nov 2014 19:55 ET  USD/Asia Subdued by Lukewarm U.S. Data -- Asia -2-\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 . The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 26, 2014 19:55 ET (00:55 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141127eabr0000w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
