\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Yen rebound lifts regional peers; Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  down for week\b0\par\par\uc2 538 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 November 2014\par 09:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Updates prices. For midday report, double-click\par  )\par     SINGAPORE, Nov 21 (Reuters) - Emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose\par on Friday as the yen rebounded after Japan's Finance Minister\par Taro Aso warned against the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent swift fall,\par although most regional units were set for another week of\par losses.\par     The yen gained as Aso earlier described the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weakening as "too rapid," but ruled out \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par to halt the slide. \par     The rebound caused investors to cover short positions in\par emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Still, most regional units were poised to post weekly\par losses, led by the South Korean won, as the yen hit a\par seven-year low against the dollar on Thursday.\par     The won ended the week down 1.2 percent against the dollar,\par its fourth week of declines, according to Thomson Reuters data.\par That was the longest streak of weekly losses since May 2013.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities were suspected of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to check the won's strength against the yen\par  on concerns it would erode the competitiveness of\par exporters against their Japanese rivals.\par     The Taiwan dollar fell 0.8 percent with the\par island's exporters also seen vulnerable to weakness in the yen\par and the won. The Indian rupee has eased 0.2 percent so\par far this week.\par     Malaysia's ringgit has slid 0.1 percent, while the\par Philippine peso closed the week down 0.1 percent.\par     The Indonesian rupiah stood firm in the face of\par falls in regional peers, having risen 0.7 percent.\par     Indonesia's President Joko Widodo on Monday announced a\par long-awaited decision to raise fuel prices and free up funds to\par rejuvenate Southeast Asia's biggest economy. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on\par Tuesday hiked interest rates to temper an expected upsurge in\par inflation following the fuel price hike.\par     China's yuan has gained 0.1 percent on\par expectations of inflows due to a new link between the Hong Kong\par and Shanghai stock exchanges.\par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0800 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       117.54         118.20       +0.56\par   Sing dlr        1.2970         1.2999       +0.22\par   Taiwan dlr      31.000         31.015       +0.05\par   Korean won     1112.09        1115.10       +0.27\par   Baht             32.73          32.81       +0.26\par   Peso             44.98          45.07       +0.20\par   Rupiah        12130.00       12170.00       +0.33\par   Rupee            61.85          61.94       +0.15\par   Ringgit         3.3500         3.3668       +0.50\par   Yuan            6.1250         6.1245       -0.01\par  \par   Change so far in 2014\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       117.54         105.28      -10.43\par   Sing dlr        1.2970         1.2632       -2.61\par   Taiwan dlr      31.000         29.950       -3.39\par   Korean won     1112.09        1055.40       -5.10\par   Baht             32.73          32.86       +0.41\par   Peso             44.98          44.40       -1.30\par   Rupiah        12130.00       12160.00       +0.25\par   Rupee            61.85          61.80       -0.08\par   Ringgit         3.3500         3.2755       -2.22\par   Yuan            6.1250         6.0539       -1.16\par  \par  (Reporting by Jongwoo Cheon; Editing by Prateek Chatterjee)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-11-21T09:35:26.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141121eabl008ki\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (South Korea near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 21/08/2023\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\asp